 {"w":"identisch","kind":"a","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"identical with","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit ist das identisch?","decoys":["bei + Dat.","von + Dat.","an + Dat.","für + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Die Kopie ist {{mit}} dem Original identisch.","en":"The copy is identical to the original."},{"de":"Seine Aussage ist {{mit}} meiner identisch.","en":"His statement is identical to mine."},{"de":"Der Entwurf ist {{mit}} dem ersten Plan fast identisch.","en":"The draft is almost identical to the first plan."}]},
 {"w":"genervt","kind":"a","prep":"von","case":"Dat","en":"annoyed by, fed up with","lv":"B1","da":"davon","wo":"Wovon bist du genervt? / Von wem bist du genervt?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","mit + Dat.","für + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Ich bin {{von}} diesem Lärm genervt.","en":"I'm annoyed by this noise."},{"de":"Sie ist {{von}} ihrem Chef genervt.","en":"She is fed up with her boss."},{"de":"Wir sind {{von}} der ständigen Warterei genervt.","en":"We are fed up with the constant waiting."}]},
 {"w":"entschlossen","kind":"a","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"determined to, resolved to","lv":"B2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu ist er entschlossen?","decoys":["mit + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","in + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Er ist {{zu}} einem Neuanfang entschlossen.","en":"He is determined to make a fresh start."},{"de":"Wir sind {{zu}} allem entschlossen.","en":"We are prepared to do anything."},{"de":"Sie ist {{zu}} einer Veränderung fest entschlossen.","en":"She is firmly resolved to make a change."}]},
 {"w":"kommen","kind":"v","prep":"aus","case":"Dat","en":"to come from (origin)","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein da-Wort; meist: von dort / daher)","wo":"Woher kommst du? / Aus welchem Land kommt sie?","decoys":["von + Dat.","in + Dat.","bei + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"kommen aus + Dat. = origin (country, city, home). kommen von + Dat. = where someone has just been (Ich komme gerade von der Arbeit). English \"from\" is not automatically von.","ex":[{"de":"Meine Frau kommt ursprünglich {{aus}} Italien.","en":"My wife is originally from Italy."},{"de":"Dieser Käse kommt {{aus}} der Schweiz.","en":"This cheese comes from Switzerland."},{"de":"Kommt ihr {{aus}} derselben Stadt?","en":"Do you come from the same city?"}]},
 {"w":"wohnen","kind":"v","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"to live with (someone), at someone's place","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: bei ihm / bei ihr)","wo":"Bei wem wohnst du?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","nach + Dat.","für + Akk."],"note":"wohnen bei = living in someone else's home (parents, host family). mit + Dat. = sharing a home as equals, only with zusammen (Ich wohne mit meinem Freund zusammen).","ex":[{"de":"Ich wohne noch {{bei}} meinen Eltern.","en":"I still live with my parents."},{"de":"Im Moment wohnt mein Bruder {{bei}} seiner Freundin.","en":"At the moment my brother is living at his girlfriend's."},{"de":"Wohnst du {{bei}} deiner Tante oder hast du eine eigene Wohnung?","en":"Do you live with your aunt, or do you have your own flat?"}]},
 {"w":"übernachten","kind":"v","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"to stay overnight at (someone's place)","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: bei ihm / bei ihr)","wo":"Bei wem übernachtest du?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","für + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"übernachten bei + Dat. = at a person's home. For places: übernachten in einem Hotel / auf einem Campingplatz.","ex":[{"de":"Heute Nacht übernachte ich {{bei}} meiner Freundin.","en":"Tonight I'm staying overnight at my girlfriend's."},{"de":"Kann ich {{bei}} dir übernachten?","en":"Can I stay at your place overnight?"},{"de":"Auf der Reise haben wir {{bei}} Bekannten übernachtet.","en":"On the trip we stayed with acquaintances."}]},
 {"w":"arbeiten","kind":"v","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"to work for, to work at (a company, an employer)","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein da-Wort; meist: dort)","wo":"Bei welcher Firma arbeitest du? / Bei wem arbeitet er?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","um + Akk.","nach + Dat."],"alt":["für + Akk.","in + Dat."],"note":"arbeiten bei + Dat. = employer. für + Akk. = on behalf of; in + Dat. = place or department (in einem Büro); an + Dat. = a task (an einem Projekt).","ex":[{"de":"Mein Vater arbeitet {{bei}} der Post.","en":"My father works for the post office."},{"de":"Sie arbeitet seit zwei Jahren {{bei}} einer großen Versicherung.","en":"She has been working for a big insurance company for two years."},{"de":"Arbeitest du schon lange {{bei}} dieser Firma?","en":"Have you been working at this company for a long time?"}]},
 {"w":"einsteigen","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to get on, to get in (a vehicle)","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein da-Wort; meist: „Steig ein!“)","wo":"In welchen Zug steigst du ein?","decoys":["in + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"einsteigen in + Akk. (wohin?) is the counterpart of aussteigen aus + Dat. (woraus?).","ex":[{"de":"Wir steigen am Hauptbahnhof {{in}} den Zug nach Hamburg ein.","en":"We get on the train to Hamburg at the main station."},{"de":"Bitte steigen Sie vorne {{in}} den Bus ein.","en":"Please get on the bus at the front."},{"de":"Sie ist schnell {{in}} ihr Auto eingestiegen.","en":"She quickly got into her car."}]},
 {"w":"aussteigen","kind":"v","prep":"aus","case":"Dat","en":"to get off, to get out of (a vehicle)","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein da-Wort; meist: „Steig aus!“)","wo":"Aus welchem Bus steigst du aus?","decoys":["von + Dat.","in + Akk.","bei + Dat.","zu + Dat."],"note":"aus dem Auto / Bus / Zug aussteigen. English \"get off\" is not von. (Only for bike or horse: vom Fahrrad / Pferd absteigen.)","ex":[{"de":"Wir steigen in Mainz {{aus}} dem Zug aus.","en":"We get off the train in Mainz."},{"de":"Sie ist schnell {{aus}} dem Auto ausgestiegen.","en":"She quickly got out of the car."},{"de":"Bitte steigen Sie hier {{aus}} der Straßenbahn aus.","en":"Please get off the tram here."}]},
 {"w":"ankommen","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to arrive in (a city, a country)","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein da-Wort; meist: dort)","wo":"Wo kommt ihr an? / In welcher Stadt kommt der Zug an?","decoys":["in + Akk.","nach + Dat.","zu + Dat.","an + Akk."],"note":"ankommen in + Dat. = arriving in a city or country. At a specific point: ankommen an + Dat. (am Bahnhof, am Flughafen).","ex":[{"de":"Der Zug kommt um 18 Uhr {{in}} Berlin an.","en":"The train arrives in Berlin at 6 p.m."},{"de":"Wir sind gestern Abend {{in}} Wien angekommen.","en":"We arrived in Vienna yesterday evening."},{"de":"Wann kommst du {{in}} München an?","en":"When do you arrive in Munich?"}]},
 {"w":"sich melden","kind":"v","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"to get in touch with, to contact","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: bei ihm / bei ihr)","wo":"Bei wem meldest du dich?","decoys":["an + Akk.","von + Dat.","mit + Dat.","nach + Dat."],"note":"sich bei jdm. melden = get in touch / report to someone (Ich melde mich = I'll call/write you).","ex":[{"de":"Ich melde mich morgen {{bei}} dir.","en":"I'll get in touch with you tomorrow."},{"de":"Sie hat sich noch nicht {{bei}} mir gemeldet.","en":"She hasn't contacted me yet."},{"de":"Melden Sie sich bitte {{bei}} Ihrem Lehrer.","en":"Please report to your teacher."}]},
 {"w":"sich verabreden","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to arrange to meet (someone)","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: mit ihm / mit ihr)","wo":"Mit wem verabredest du dich?","decoys":["nach + Dat.","an + Akk.","von + Dat.","über + Akk."],"note":"Like sich treffen mit: the person is always mit + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe mich heute Abend {{mit}} meiner Freundin verabredet.","en":"I've arranged to meet my girlfriend this evening."},{"de":"Am Samstag verabrede ich mich {{mit}} meinen Kollegen.","en":"On Saturday I'm arranging to meet my colleagues."},{"de":"Hast du dich schon {{mit}} deiner Schwester verabredet?","en":"Have you already arranged to meet your sister?"}]},
 {"w":"sich anmelden","kind":"v","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"to sign up for, to register for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür meldest du dich an?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Akk.","um + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"alt":["zu + Dat."],"note":"sich für / zu einem Kurs anmelden. The institution takes bei: sich bei der Volkshochschule anmelden.","ex":[{"de":"Ich möchte mich {{für}} den Deutschkurs anmelden.","en":"I'd like to sign up for the German course."},{"de":"Hast du dich schon {{für}} die Prüfung angemeldet?","en":"Have you already registered for the exam?"},{"de":"Wir haben uns {{für}} einen Kochkurs angemeldet.","en":"We have signed up for a cooking course."}]},
 {"w":"reden","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to talk about","lv":"A2","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber redet ihr? / Über wen redet ihr?","decoys":["um + Akk.","an + Akk.","auf + Akk.","über + Dat."],"note":"reden über + Akk. = the topic. The person you talk to: reden mit + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Die Kinder reden die ganze Zeit {{über}} Fußball.","en":"The children talk about football all the time."},{"de":"Wir haben gestern lange {{über}} unsere Reise geredet.","en":"We talked about our trip for a long time yesterday."},{"de":"Sie redet nicht gern {{über}} ihre Probleme.","en":"She doesn't like talking about her problems."}],"alt":["von + Dat."]},
 {"w":"ausgeben","kind":"v","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"to spend (money) on","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür gibst du dein Geld aus?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Akk.","zu + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"English \"spend ON\" is not auf: Geld für etwas ausgeben.","ex":[{"de":"Ich gebe viel Geld {{für}} Bücher aus.","en":"I spend a lot of money on books."},{"de":"Wie viel gebt ihr im Monat {{für}} das Essen aus?","en":"How much do you spend on food per month?"},{"de":"Sie hat 200 Euro {{für}} die Schuhe ausgegeben.","en":"She spent 200 euros on the shoes."}]},
 {"w":"fahren","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to go by, to travel by (means of transport)","lv":"A2","da":"damit","wo":"Womit fährst du zur Arbeit?","decoys":["von + Dat.","bei + Dat.","für + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"mit + Dat. names the means of transport (mit dem Bus fahren). English \"by bus\" is not bei or von.","ex":[{"de":"Ich fahre jeden Tag {{mit}} dem Bus zur Arbeit.","en":"I take the bus to work every day."},{"de":"Wir sind {{mit}} dem Zug nach Wien gefahren.","en":"We travelled to Vienna by train."},{"de":"Meine Schwester fährt lieber {{mit}} dem Fahrrad.","en":"My sister prefers to go by bike."}]},
 {"w":"bezahlen","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to pay by, to pay with","lv":"A2","da":"damit","wo":"Womit bezahlst du?","decoys":["durch + Akk.","bei + Dat.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat."],"alt":["per + Akk."],"note":"mit Karte / mit Bargeld. English \"pay BY card\" is not bei or durch (durch only in formal phrases: durch Überweisung). (per Karte is also correct.)","ex":[{"de":"Kann ich hier {{mit}} meiner Karte bezahlen?","en":"Can I pay with my card here?"},{"de":"Ich bezahle meistens {{mit}} Bargeld.","en":"I mostly pay in cash."},{"de":"Er hat die Rechnung {{mit}} einem großen Schein bezahlt.","en":"He paid the bill with a large banknote."}]},
 {"w":"beginnen","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to begin with, to start with","lv":"A2","da":"damit","wo":"Womit beginnt der Kurs? / Womit beginnst du den Tag?","decoys":["von + Dat.","zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Same pattern as anfangen mit + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Der Unterricht beginnt {{mit}} einer Wiederholung.","en":"The lesson begins with a review."},{"de":"Wir beginnen heute {{mit}} Kapitel fünf.","en":"Today we start with chapter five."},{"de":"Er beginnt den Tag immer {{mit}} einem Kaffee.","en":"He always starts the day with a coffee."}]},
 {"w":"teilen","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to share with","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: mit ihm / mit ihr)","wo":"Mit wem teilst du das Zimmer?","decoys":["bei + Dat.","zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"etwas mit jdm. teilen. Also reflexive: Wir teilen uns die Wohnung mit einem Freund.","ex":[{"de":"Ich teile mein Zimmer {{mit}} meiner Schwester.","en":"I share my room with my sister."},{"de":"Sie teilt gern ihr Essen {{mit}} den Kindern.","en":"She likes sharing her food with the children."},{"de":"Wir haben die Pizza {{mit}} unseren Nachbarn geteilt.","en":"We shared the pizza with our neighbours."}]},
 {"w":"wählen","kind":"v","prep":"zwischen","case":"Dat","en":"to choose between","lv":"A2","da":"– (kein gebräuchliches da-Wort; meist: zwischen beiden)","wo":"Zwischen welchen Angeboten kannst du wählen?","decoys":["zwischen + Akk.","von + Dat.","bei + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"zwischen + Dat. here (no movement). Choosing from a larger group: wählen aus + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Du kannst {{zwischen}} Tee und Kaffee wählen.","en":"You can choose between tea and coffee."},{"de":"Sie muss {{zwischen}} zwei Jobs wählen.","en":"She has to choose between two jobs."},{"de":"Wir mussten {{zwischen}} dem Meer und den Bergen wählen.","en":"We had to choose between the sea and the mountains."}]},
 {"w":"zeigen","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to point at, to point to","lv":"A2","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf zeigt er? / Auf wen zeigt sie?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","bei + Dat.","um + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"zeigen auf + Akk. = point at. Showing something to someone: jdm. etwas zeigen (Dat. + Akk., no preposition).","ex":[{"de":"Das Kind zeigt {{auf}} den Hund.","en":"The child points at the dog."},{"de":"Er zeigte mit dem Finger {{auf}} das Haus.","en":"He pointed at the house with his finger."},{"de":"Warum zeigen alle {{auf}} mich?","en":"Why is everyone pointing at me?"}]},
 {"w":"vorbeigehen","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"to walk past, to pass (by)","lv":"A2","da":"daran","wo":"Woran gehst du vorbei? / An wem geht er vorbei?","decoys":["an + Akk.","nach + Dat.","über + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"an etwas vorbeigehen / vorbeifahren: the preposition an + Dat. stands before the noun, the particle vorbei comes at the end.","ex":[{"de":"Gehen Sie {{an}} der Kirche vorbei und dann links.","en":"Walk past the church and then turn left."},{"de":"Sie ging {{an}} mir vorbei, ohne zu grüßen.","en":"She walked past me without saying hello."},{"de":"Jeden Morgen gehe ich {{an}} einem kleinen Park vorbei.","en":"Every morning I walk past a small park."}]},
 {"w":"der Brief","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"letter to","lv":"A2","da":"– (an Personen: an ihn / an sie)","wo":"An wen schreibst du den Brief?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","bei + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Brief an + Akk. = the addressee. Brief von + Dat. = the sender.","ex":[{"de":"Ich schreibe einen Brief {{an}} meine Großeltern.","en":"I'm writing a letter to my grandparents."},{"de":"Der Brief {{an}} den Chef muss heute noch raus.","en":"The letter to the boss has to go out today."},{"de":"Hast du den Brief {{an}} die Schule schon abgeschickt?","en":"Have you already sent the letter to the school?"}]},
 {"w":"die Einladung","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"invitation to","lv":"A2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu hast du eine Einladung bekommen?","decoys":["an + Dat.","über + Akk.","auf + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Same pattern as the verb einladen zu + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Danke für die Einladung {{zu}} deiner Party!","en":"Thank you for the invitation to your party!"},{"de":"Wir haben eine Einladung {{zu}} einer Hochzeit bekommen.","en":"We have received an invitation to a wedding."},{"de":"Die Einladung {{zu}} unserem Fest kam per E-Mail.","en":"The invitation to our party came by email."}]},
 {"w":"die Zeit","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"time for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür hast du keine Zeit? / Für wen hast du Zeit?","decoys":["über + Akk.","an + Akk.","bei + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Zeit für + Akk. (a person or event). Before an activity noun also zu: keine Zeit zum Lesen.","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe heute leider keine Zeit {{für}} dich.","en":"Unfortunately I have no time for you today."},{"de":"Nimm dir mehr Zeit {{für}} deine Familie!","en":"Take more time for your family!"},{"de":"Hast du morgen Zeit {{für}} einen Kaffee?","en":"Do you have time for a coffee tomorrow?"}]},
 {"w":"die Karte","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"ticket for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür brauchst du die Karten?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","bei + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Karte / Eintrittskarte für + Akk. = ticket for an event (also: Karten zum Konzert). English \"ticket FOR\" matches here, unlike many other prepositions.","ex":[{"de":"Ich brauche zwei Karten {{für}} das Konzert am Freitag.","en":"I need two tickets for the concert on Friday."},{"de":"Wir haben Karten {{für}} das Fußballspiel bekommen.","en":"We got tickets for the football match."},{"de":"Gibt es noch Karten {{für}} das Theater heute Abend?","en":"Are there still tickets for the theatre tonight?"}],"alt":["zu + Dat."]},
 {"w":"der Glückwunsch","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"congratulations on","lv":"A2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu gratulierst du?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","an + Dat.","bei + Dat."],"note":"English \"congratulations ON\" is neither auf nor über. Same pattern as gratulieren zu + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Herzlichen Glückwunsch {{zu}} deinem Geburtstag!","en":"Happy birthday! (lit. congratulations on your birthday)"},{"de":"Meinen Glückwunsch {{zu}} deiner neuen Wohnung!","en":"Congratulations on your new flat!"},{"de":"Meine besten Glückwünsche {{zu}} deinem neuen Job!","en":"Congratulations on your new job!"}]},
 {"w":"die Hilfe","kind":"n","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"help with","lv":"A2","da":"dabei","wo":"Wobei brauchst du Hilfe?","decoys":["an + Dat.","um + Akk.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Same pattern as the verb helfen bei + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Ich brauche Hilfe {{bei}} meinen Hausaufgaben.","en":"I need help with my homework."},{"de":"Danke für deine Hilfe {{bei}} unserem Umzug!","en":"Thanks for your help with our move!"},{"de":"Sie bietet ihren Nachbarn Hilfe {{bei}} der Gartenarbeit an.","en":"She offers her neighbours help with the gardening."}]},
 {"w":"das Gespräch","kind":"n","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"conversation with","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: mit ihm / mit ihr)","wo":"Mit wem hattest du ein Gespräch?","decoys":["gegen + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Gespräch mit + Dat. = the person; Gespräch über + Akk. = the topic.","ex":[{"de":"Ich hatte gestern ein langes Gespräch {{mit}} meinem Chef.","en":"I had a long conversation with my boss yesterday."},{"de":"Das Gespräch {{mit}} dem Arzt war kurz, aber sehr freundlich.","en":"The talk with the doctor was short but very friendly."},{"de":"Hast du schon ein Gespräch {{mit}} deiner Lehrerin geführt?","en":"Have you already had a talk with your teacher?"}]},
 {"w":"der Termin","kind":"n","prep":"bei","case":"Dat","en":"appointment with (a doctor, hairdresser, office)","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: bei ihm / bei ihr)","wo":"Bei wem hast du einen Termin?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"einen Termin bei + Dat. (doctor, hairdresser, bank). English \"appointment WITH\" is usually bei here; mit + Dat. is used for a meeting with a partner (Termin mit dem Chef).","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe morgen einen Termin {{bei}} der Zahnärztin.","en":"I have an appointment with the dentist tomorrow."},{"de":"Wir haben um drei Uhr einen Termin {{bei}} der Bank.","en":"We have an appointment at the bank at three o'clock."},{"de":"Sie braucht bald einen Termin {{bei}} einem Augenarzt.","en":"She needs an appointment with an eye doctor soon."}]},
 {"w":"die Verabredung","kind":"n","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"date, appointment to meet (with a person)","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: mit ihm / mit ihr)","wo":"Mit wem hast du eine Verabredung?","decoys":["an + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Compare: der Termin bei + Dat. (doctor, office) vs. die Verabredung mit + Dat. (private meeting).","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe heute Abend eine Verabredung {{mit}} einer Freundin.","en":"I have plans with a friend this evening."},{"de":"Hast du morgen eine Verabredung {{mit}} deinem Freund?","en":"Are you meeting your boyfriend tomorrow?"},{"de":"Die Verabredung {{mit}} meinen Kollegen habe ich vergessen.","en":"I forgot about the meeting with my colleagues."}]},
 {"w":"die Frage","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"question about (a topic or text)","lv":"A2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu hast du eine Frage?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Frage zu + Dat. = about a topic. Frage nach + Dat. = asking for something (die Frage nach dem Weg). Frage an + Akk. = to a person (Frage an den Lehrer).","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe eine Frage {{zu}} dieser Aufgabe.","en":"I have a question about this exercise."},{"de":"Gibt es noch Fragen {{zu}} diesem Text?","en":"Are there any more questions about this text?"},{"de":"Sie hat eine Frage {{zu}} ihrer Rechnung.","en":"She has a question about her bill."}]},
 {"w":"der Gruß","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"greeting to, regards to","lv":"A2","da":"– (an Personen: an ihn / an sie)","wo":"An wen schickst du Grüße?","decoys":["über + Akk.","an + Dat.","bei + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Gruß / Grüße an + Akk. = to whom. Grüße von + Dat. = from whom.","ex":[{"de":"Bitte bestell einen schönen Gruß {{an}} deine Eltern!","en":"Please give my best regards to your parents!"},{"de":"Sie schickt einen Gruß {{an}} ihre Freunde in Berlin.","en":"She sends greetings to her friends in Berlin."},{"de":"Liebe Grüße {{an}} euch alle!","en":"Best wishes to all of you!"}]},
 {"w":"böse","kind":"a","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"angry at, cross with","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: auf ihn / auf sie)","wo":"Auf wen bist du böse?","decoys":["in + Akk.","an + Akk.","von + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"böse auf + Akk. (person). Colloquially also mit jdm. böse sein. Similar: wütend auf. Also possible without preposition: jdm. böse sein (Bist du mir noch böse?).","ex":[{"de":"Bist du noch böse {{auf}} mich?","en":"Are you still angry with me?"},{"de":"Sie ist böse {{auf}} ihren Bruder, weil er ihr Handy genommen hat.","en":"She is angry with her brother because he took her phone."},{"de":"Mein Vater war lange böse {{auf}} mich.","en":"My father was angry with me for a long time."}],"alt":["mit + Dat."]},
 {"w":"schlecht","kind":"a","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"bad at (a subject)","lv":"A2","da":"darin","wo":"In welchem Fach bist du schlecht? / Worin bist du schlecht?","decoys":["in + Akk.","über + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Dat."],"note":"Same pattern as gut in + Dat. English \"bad AT\" is not an.","ex":[{"de":"Ich bin schlecht {{in}} Mathe.","en":"I'm bad at maths."},{"de":"Sie ist schlecht {{in}} den meisten Fächern.","en":"She is bad at most subjects."},{"de":"Mein Bruder war früher schlecht {{in}} Sport.","en":"My brother used to be bad at P.E."}]},
 {"w":"lieb","kind":"a","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"kind to, nice to","lv":"A2","da":"– (nur Personen: zu ihm / zu ihr)","wo":"Zu wem bist du lieb?","decoys":["mit + Dat.","für + Akk.","an + Dat.","bei + Dat."],"note":"Same pattern as nett zu and freundlich zu.","ex":[{"de":"Sei lieb {{zu}} deiner kleinen Schwester!","en":"Be nice to your little sister!"},{"de":"Die Nachbarn waren immer sehr lieb {{zu}} uns.","en":"The neighbours were always very kind to us."},{"de":"Der Hund ist lieb {{zu}} den Kindern.","en":"The dog is gentle with the children."}]},
 {"w":"gut","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"good for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das gut? / Für wen ist das gut?","decoys":["an + Akk.","über + Akk.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"gut für + Akk. = beneficial for. (gut zu jdm. = kind to someone; gut in + Dat. = skilled at.)","ex":[{"de":"Obst und Gemüse sind gut {{für}} die Gesundheit.","en":"Fruit and vegetables are good for your health."},{"de":"Ein Spaziergang ist gut {{für}} den Rücken.","en":"A walk is good for your back."},{"de":"Das ist nicht gut {{für}} dich.","en":"That is not good for you."}]},
 {"w":"schlecht","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"bad for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das schlecht? / Für wen ist das schlecht?","decoys":["an + Akk.","über + Akk.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Compare: schlecht in + Dat. (bad at a subject) vs. schlecht für + Akk. (harmful, unsuitable for).","ex":[{"de":"Rauchen ist schlecht {{für}} die Gesundheit.","en":"Smoking is bad for your health."},{"de":"Zu viel Zucker ist schlecht {{für}} die Zähne.","en":"Too much sugar is bad for your teeth."},{"de":"Das Wetter ist schlecht {{für}} einen Ausflug.","en":"The weather is bad for an outing."}]},
 {"w":"schwer","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"hard for, difficult for","lv":"A2","da":"dafür","wo":"Für wen ist das schwer?","decoys":["an + Akk.","bei + Dat.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"schwer / leicht für + Akk. = for whom something is hard or easy.","ex":[{"de":"Die Prüfung war sehr schwer {{für}} die Schüler.","en":"The exam was very hard for the students."},{"de":"Die Aufgabe ist zu schwer {{für}} mich.","en":"The exercise is too hard for me."},{"de":"Deutsche Artikel sind schwer {{für}} viele Lerner.","en":"German articles are hard for many learners."}]},
 {"w":"wehtun","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to hurt, to ache","lv":"A2","note":"The person is Dativ, the aching body part is the subject (Nominativ). So: Mir tut der Kopf weh, not \"Ich tue Kopf weh\".","ex":[{"de":"Mir tut der Kopf weh.","en":"My head hurts."},{"de":"Tut dir der Rücken weh?","en":"Does your back hurt?"},{"de":"Dem Kind haben nach dem Laufen die Füße wehgetan.","en":"The child's feet hurt after running."}]},
 {"w":"leidtun","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to be sorry, to feel sorry for","lv":"A2","note":"Es tut mir leid. = I'm sorry. The person who is sorry is Dativ (mir, dir, ihm).","ex":[{"de":"Es tut mir leid, dass ich zu spät bin.","en":"I'm sorry that I'm late."},{"de":"Tut es dir nicht leid?","en":"Aren't you sorry?"},{"de":"Die Kinder tun mir leid, weil sie so lange warten müssen.","en":"I feel sorry for the children because they have to wait so long."}]},
 {"w":"passieren","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to happen (to someone)","lv":"A2","note":"The person it happens to is Dativ. Perfekt with sein: ist passiert.","ex":[{"de":"Was ist dir denn passiert?","en":"What happened to you?"},{"de":"Ihm ist gestern ein Unfall passiert.","en":"An accident happened to him yesterday."},{"de":"Mir passiert das leider ziemlich oft.","en":"Unfortunately that happens to me quite often."}]},
 {"w":"stehen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to suit (clothes, colours)","lv":"A2","note":"Here stehen means \"suit\": jdm. steht etwas gut. Not the same as passen (size) or gefallen (liking).","ex":[{"de":"Die rote Jacke steht dir wirklich gut.","en":"The red jacket really suits you."},{"de":"Steht mir diese Farbe gut?","en":"Does this colour suit me?"},{"de":"Der neue Haarschnitt steht ihr sehr gut.","en":"The new haircut suits her very well."}]},
 {"w":"heiraten","kind":"c","case":"Akk","en":"to marry","lv":"A2","note":"heiraten + Akk., no preposition (not \"heiraten mit\"). The adjective is different: verheiratet mit + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Meine Schwester heiratet nächstes Jahr einen Franzosen.","en":"My sister is marrying a Frenchman next year."},{"de":"Er hat vor zwei Jahren seine Kollegin geheiratet.","en":"Two years ago he married his colleague."},{"de":"Willst du mich heiraten?","en":"Will you marry me?"}]},
 {"w":"besuchen","kind":"c","case":"Akk","en":"to visit","lv":"A2","note":"jdn. besuchen + Akk., no preposition. The noun is different: der Besuch bei + Dat.","ex":[{"de":"Ich besuche meine Oma jeden Sonntag.","en":"I visit my grandma every Sunday."},{"de":"Im Sommer besuchen wir unsere Freunde in Wien.","en":"In summer we are visiting our friends in Vienna."},{"de":"Hast du das Museum schon besucht?","en":"Have you already visited the museum?"}]},
 {"w":"brauchen","kind":"c","case":"Akk","en":"to need","lv":"A2","note":"brauchen + Akk., no preposition for the thing needed (not \"brauchen an\"). A purpose can be added: etwas für etwas brauchen.","ex":[{"de":"Ich brauche einen neuen Pullover.","en":"I need a new jumper."},{"de":"Wie viel Zeit brauchst du noch?","en":"How much more time do you need?"},{"de":"Wir haben den Schirm gestern gebraucht.","en":"We needed the umbrella yesterday."}]},
 {"w":"abholen","kind":"c","case":"Akk","en":"to pick up, to collect","lv":"A2","note":"jdn. / etwas abholen + Akk. (separable verb).","ex":[{"de":"Ich hole dich um acht Uhr am Bahnhof ab.","en":"I'll pick you up at the station at eight o'clock."},{"de":"Wer holt die Kinder von der Schule ab?","en":"Who picks the children up from school?"},{"de":"Er hat das Paket gestern bei der Post abgeholt.","en":"He collected the parcel at the post office yesterday."}]},
 {"w":"vergessen","kind":"c","case":"Akk","en":"to forget","lv":"A2","note":"In Standard German vergessen takes its object directly (+ Akk.), no preposition; \"forget ABOUT\" is not an or über. (Regional, esp. Austria: vergessen auf.)","ex":[{"de":"Ich habe meinen Schlüssel vergessen.","en":"I've forgotten my key."},{"de":"Hast du den Termin schon wieder vergessen?","en":"Have you forgotten the appointment again?"},{"de":"Vergiss deine Hausaufgaben nicht!","en":"Don't forget your homework!"}]},
 {"w":"anknüpfen","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"to build on, to take up (a thread)","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran knüpft der Autor an? / An wen knüpft er an?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","in + Akk.","über + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Separable: an etwas anknüpfen. Also transitive: ein Gespräch anknüpfen.","ex":[{"de":"Der Roman knüpft {{an}} die Tradition des 19. Jahrhunderts an.","en":"The novel builds on the tradition of the 19th century."},{"de":"Wir können {{an}} die Ergebnisse der letzten Studie anknüpfen.","en":"We can build on the results of the last study."},{"de":"Die Ministerin knüpfte in ihrer Rede {{an}} frühere Ankündigungen an.","en":"In her speech the minister took up earlier announcements."}]},
 {"w":"beharren","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Dat","en":"to insist on, to persist in","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf beharrt sie?","decoys":["für + Akk.","an + Dat.","über + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"alt":["bei + Dat."],"note":"Formal; stronger than bestehen auf. Usually auf + Dat. (auf seiner Meinung beharren); bei is the rarer variant.","ex":[{"de":"Der Verband beharrt {{auf}} seiner Forderung nach höheren Löhnen.","en":"The association insists on its demand for higher wages."},{"de":"Er beharrte {{auf}} einer schriftlichen Bestätigung.","en":"He insisted on written confirmation."},{"de":"Wer {{auf}} seinem Standpunkt beharrt, wird kaum einen Kompromiss finden.","en":"Anyone who sticks to his position will hardly find a compromise."}]},
 {"w":"rekurrieren","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to refer back to, to fall back on (formal)","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf rekurriert die Autorin?","decoys":["an + Akk.","zu + Dat.","über + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"Bildungssprache. Close to sich beziehen auf and zurückgreifen auf.","ex":[{"de":"Die Argumentation rekurriert {{auf}} ältere Theorien der Sozialpsychologie.","en":"The argument refers back to older theories of social psychology."},{"de":"Der Gutachter rekurriert in seiner Stellungnahme {{auf}} ein Urteil von 2015.","en":"In his statement the expert refers back to a 2015 ruling."},{"de":"Viele Politiker rekurrieren {{auf}} die Idee des Gemeinwohls.","en":"Many politicians appeal to the idea of the common good."}]},
 {"w":"fußen","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Dat","en":"to be based on, to rest on","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf fußt die Theorie?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","aus + Dat.","an + Dat.","von + Dat."],"note":"More literary than basieren auf / beruhen auf; same case (Dat.).","ex":[{"de":"Das Urteil fußt {{auf}} den Aussagen mehrerer Zeugen.","en":"The verdict is based on the statements of several witnesses."},{"de":"Seine Skepsis fußt {{auf}} jahrelanger Erfahrung.","en":"His scepticism rests on years of experience."},{"de":"Die Studie fußt {{auf}} einer repräsentativen Stichprobe.","en":"The study is based on a representative sample."}]},
 {"w":"kulminieren","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to culminate in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin kulminierte der Streit?","decoys":["in + Akk.","zu + Dat.","auf + Dat.","für + Akk."],"note":"Bildungssprache. Dat. (in einem Streit), like gipfeln in.","ex":[{"de":"Der Konflikt kulminierte {{in}} einem offenen Streit zwischen den Partnern.","en":"The conflict culminated in an open dispute between the partners."},{"de":"Die Proteste kulminierten {{in}} der Besetzung des Rathauses.","en":"The protests culminated in the occupation of the town hall."},{"de":"Ihre Karriere kulminierte {{in}} der Verleihung des Nobelpreises.","en":"Her career culminated in being awarded the Nobel Prize."}]},
 {"w":"gipfeln","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to culminate in, to peak in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin gipfelte die Kritik?","decoys":["in + Akk.","zu + Dat.","auf + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"Dat. (in einem Eklat). Close to kulminieren in.","ex":[{"de":"Die Verhandlungen gipfelten {{in}} einem Eklat.","en":"The negotiations culminated in a scandal."},{"de":"Seine Kritik gipfelte {{in}} dem Vorwurf, die Regierung belüge das Volk.","en":"His criticism culminated in the accusation that the government was lying to the people."},{"de":"Der Nachbarschaftsstreit gipfelte {{in}} einer Anzeige wegen Beleidigung.","en":"The neighbourhood dispute culminated in a criminal complaint for insult."}]},
 {"w":"münden","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to lead into, to flow into, to end up in","lv":"C1","da":"darin (v. a. mit dass-Satz: Das mündete darin, dass …)","wo":"Wohin mündet der Rhein? / In was mündet die Debatte? (ugs.)","decoys":["zu + Dat.","aus + Dat.","für + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Literal (rivers, streets) and figurative (talks lead into an agreement).","ex":[{"de":"Der Rhein mündet {{in}} die Nordsee.","en":"The Rhine flows into the North Sea."},{"de":"Die Diskussion mündete {{in}} einen heftigen Streit.","en":"The discussion ended in a heated quarrel."},{"de":"Die Reformen sollen {{in}} ein neues Gesetz münden.","en":"The reforms are meant to result in a new law."}]},
 {"w":"sich erstrecken","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to extend to, to apply to","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf erstreckt sich die Regelung?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","um + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Figurative: scope of a rule or suspicion. Spatial 'stretch across' is sich erstrecken über.","ex":[{"de":"Die Regelung erstreckt sich {{auf}} alle Beschäftigten im öffentlichen Dienst.","en":"The regulation applies to all employees in the public sector."},{"de":"Der Verdacht erstreckte sich auch {{auf}} seine Mitarbeiter.","en":"The suspicion also extended to his staff."},{"de":"Die Befugnisse des Beauftragten erstrecken sich nicht {{auf}} die Personalpolitik.","en":"The commissioner's powers do not extend to personnel policy."}]},
 {"w":"zurückgreifen","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to fall back on, to draw on","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf greift man zurück? / Auf wen greift man zurück?","decoys":["an + Akk.","zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Separable: auf etwas zurückgreifen.","ex":[{"de":"Im Notfall können wir {{auf}} unsere Reserven zurückgreifen.","en":"In an emergency we can fall back on our reserves."},{"de":"Die Autorin greift {{auf}} historische Quellen zurück.","en":"The author draws on historical sources."},{"de":"Bei Personalmangel greift die Klinik {{auf}} externe Pflegekräfte zurück.","en":"When short-staffed, the clinic resorts to external nursing staff."}]},
 {"w":"zusteuern","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to head for, to steer towards","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf steuert das Land zu?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Separable: auf etwas zusteuern. Literal and figurative.","ex":[{"de":"Das Unternehmen steuert {{auf}} eine Insolvenz zu.","en":"The company is heading for insolvency."},{"de":"Die Verhandlungen steuern {{auf}} eine Entscheidung zu.","en":"The negotiations are heading towards a decision."},{"de":"Das Schiff steuerte {{auf}} den Hafen zu.","en":"The ship steered towards the harbour."}]},
 {"w":"sich besinnen","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to recall; to return to (one's values)","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf besinnt sie sich?","decoys":["bei + Dat.","mit + Dat.","für + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Standard German: sich auf etwas besinnen (sich an etwas besinnen is regional). Compare sich erinnern an.","ex":[{"de":"Die Partei muss sich wieder {{auf}} ihre Grundwerte besinnen.","en":"The party must return to its core values."},{"de":"Er besann sich {{auf}} den Rat seiner Großmutter.","en":"He remembered his grandmother's advice."},{"de":"In der Krise besannen sich viele {{auf}} die Stärke der Gemeinschaft.","en":"In the crisis many people remembered the strength of the community."}]},
 {"w":"verfallen","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to lapse into, to fall into (a state)","lv":"C1","da":"– (kein gebräuchliches da-Wort)","wo":"In welchen Zustand verfiel er?","decoys":["für + Akk.","an + Dat.","von + Dat.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Fixed with states: in Panik / Schweigen / Hektik / alte Gewohnheiten verfallen. Not to be confused with verfallen + Dat. (to fall prey to) or verfallen auf (to hit upon).","ex":[{"de":"Nach der Nachricht verfiel sie {{in}} tiefes Schweigen.","en":"After the news she lapsed into deep silence."},{"de":"Viele Länder verfallen {{in}} alte Denkmuster, wenn die Krise länger anhält.","en":"Many countries slip back into old patterns of thinking when the crisis drags on."},{"de":"Er verfiel {{in}} Panik, als das Licht ausging.","en":"He fell into a panic when the lights went out."}],"sense":"to lapse into (a state)"},
 {"w":"einwirken","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to influence, to act on","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf wirkt das ein? / Auf wen wirkt er ein?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Separable: auf jdn./etwas einwirken. With people: to try to persuade or influence.","ex":[{"de":"Die Eltern versuchten, beruhigend {{auf}} das Kind einzuwirken.","en":"The parents tried to have a calming influence on the child."},{"de":"Chemikalien können {{auf}} das Grundwasser einwirken.","en":"Chemicals can affect the groundwater."},{"de":"Die Lobby wirkte intensiv {{auf}} den Gesetzgeber ein.","en":"The lobby exerted heavy influence on the legislator."}]},
 {"w":"hinwirken","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to work towards, to strive to bring about","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf wirkt die Regierung hin?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","nach + Dat.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Separable; formal. Close to hinarbeiten auf.","ex":[{"de":"Die Kommission wirkt {{auf}} eine einvernehmliche Lösung hin.","en":"The commission is working towards an amicable solution."},{"de":"Der Betriebsrat soll {{auf}} eine Senkung der Arbeitsbelastung hinwirken.","en":"The works council is to work towards reducing the workload."},{"de":"Alle Beteiligten müssen {{auf}} einen Kompromiss hinwirken.","en":"All those involved must work towards a compromise."}]},
 {"w":"sich auszeichnen","kind":"v","prep":"durch","case":"Akk","en":"to be distinguished by, to stand out for","lv":"C1","da":"dadurch","wo":"Wodurch zeichnet sich das Gebäude aus?","decoys":["aus + Dat.","zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Separable: sich durch etwas auszeichnen. Transitive auszeichnen (to award) is different: jdn. mit einem Preis auszeichnen.","ex":[{"de":"Das Gebäude zeichnet sich {{durch}} eine ungewöhnliche Fassade aus.","en":"The building is distinguished by an unusual façade."},{"de":"Ihre Arbeit zeichnet sich {{durch}} große Genauigkeit aus.","en":"Her work is characterised by great precision."},{"de":"Der Standort zeichnet sich vor allem {{durch}} seine gute Verkehrsanbindung aus.","en":"The location stands out above all for its good transport links."}]},
 {"w":"rütteln","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"to shake; to call into question","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran rüttelt er?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","um + Akk.","bei + Dat.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Literal and figurative. Idiom: Daran ist nicht zu rütteln. (There is no questioning that.)","ex":[{"de":"Der Wind rüttelte {{an}} den Fensterläden.","en":"The wind shook the shutters."},{"de":"Die Affäre rüttelt {{an}} der Glaubwürdigkeit der Regierung.","en":"The affair is shaking the government's credibility."},{"de":"Niemand darf {{an}} den Grundfesten unserer Verfassung rütteln.","en":"No one may shake the foundations of our constitution."}]},
 {"w":"sich niederschlagen","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to be reflected in, to manifest itself in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin schlägt sich das nieder?","decoys":["in + Akk.","über + Akk.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk."],"note":"Separable. Dat. because the result is where the effect becomes visible.","ex":[{"de":"Die gestiegenen Energiekosten schlagen sich {{in}} höheren Verbraucherpreisen nieder.","en":"The increased energy costs are reflected in higher consumer prices."},{"de":"Ihre Erfahrungen haben sich {{in}} diesem Roman niedergeschlagen.","en":"Her experiences found expression in this novel."},{"de":"Der Wandel schlägt sich auch {{in}} der Statistik nieder.","en":"The change also shows up in the statistics."}]},
 {"w":"sich widerspiegeln","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to be reflected in, to be mirrored in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin spiegelt sich das wider?","decoys":["in + Akk.","durch + Akk.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk."],"note":"Separable: spiegelt sich wider. Close to sich niederschlagen in.","ex":[{"de":"Die soziale Ungleichheit spiegelt sich {{in}} den Bildungsabschlüssen wider.","en":"Social inequality is reflected in educational qualifications."},{"de":"{{In}} diesem Roman spiegelt sich die Stimmung der Epoche wider.","en":"The mood of the era is mirrored in this novel."},{"de":"Die Vielfalt der Region spiegelt sich {{in}} ihrer Küche wider.","en":"The diversity of the region is reflected in its cuisine."}]},
 {"w":"sich gliedern","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to be divided into","lv":"C1","da":"– (kein gebräuchliches da-Wort)","wo":"In wie viele Teile gliedert sich das Buch?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","aus + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Akk."],"note":"Often as Zustandspassiv: ist in … gegliedert.","ex":[{"de":"Die Arbeit gliedert sich {{in}} drei Hauptteile.","en":"The thesis is divided into three main parts."},{"de":"Der Bericht ist {{in}} vier Abschnitte gegliedert.","en":"The report is divided into four sections."},{"de":"Der Kurs gliedert sich {{in}} Theorie- und Praxisphasen.","en":"The course is divided into theory and practice phases."}]},
 {"w":"ermächtigen","kind":"v","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"to authorise to","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu ermächtigt das Gesetz die Behörde?","decoys":["für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Formal, legal register; often passive (ermächtigt sein zu).","ex":[{"de":"Das Gesetz ermächtigt die Regierung {{zu}} Notmaßnahmen.","en":"The law authorises the government to take emergency measures."},{"de":"Der Vorstand ermächtigte den Geschäftsführer {{zu}} Vertragsverhandlungen.","en":"The board authorised the managing director to negotiate contracts."},{"de":"Sie wurde {{zu}} dieser Entscheidung ermächtigt.","en":"She was authorised to make this decision."}]},
 {"w":"verleiten","kind":"v","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"to tempt into, to lead (astray) to","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu verleitet das Angebot?","decoys":["für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","in + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Implies something undesirable: zu Fehlern / Leichtsinn / Übertreibungen verleiten.","ex":[{"de":"Die hohen Gewinne verleiteten ihn {{zu}} riskanten Geschäften.","en":"The high profits tempted him into risky deals."},{"de":"Lass dich nicht {{zu}} voreiligen Schlüssen verleiten!","en":"Don't be tempted into jumping to conclusions!"},{"de":"Das günstige Angebot verleitet viele {{zu}} Spontankäufen.","en":"The cheap offer tempts many people into impulse purchases."}]},
 {"w":"sich durchringen","kind":"v","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"to bring oneself to, to finally decide on","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu hat sie sich durchgerungen?","decoys":["für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Separable. Implies an inner struggle before the decision.","ex":[{"de":"Nach langem Zögern rang er sich {{zu}} einer Entschuldigung durch.","en":"After long hesitation he brought himself to apologise."},{"de":"Die Koalition konnte sich nicht {{zu}} einer Reform durchringen.","en":"The coalition could not bring itself to carry out a reform."},{"de":"Endlich hat sie sich {{zu}} diesem Schritt durchgerungen.","en":"She has finally made up her mind to take this step."}]},
 {"w":"grenzen","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"to border on","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran grenzt das?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","mit + Dat.","zu + Dat.","bei + Dat."],"note":"Figurative: an Wahnsinn / Betrug / ein Wunder grenzen. Literal use also takes Akk.","ex":[{"de":"Sein Verhalten grenzt {{an}} Rücksichtslosigkeit.","en":"His behaviour borders on recklessness."},{"de":"Das Grundstück grenzt direkt {{an}} einen Wald.","en":"The plot borders directly on a forest."},{"de":"Die Schweiz grenzt {{an}} fünf Länder.","en":"Switzerland borders five countries."}]},
 {"w":"hadern","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to wrestle with, to be at odds with","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit hadert er? / Mit wem hadert sie?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","für + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Common: mit dem Schicksal / mit sich selbst hadern.","ex":[{"de":"Er haderte lange {{mit}} seinem Schicksal.","en":"For a long time he was at odds with his fate."},{"de":"Viele Wähler hadern {{mit}} der Politik der Regierung.","en":"Many voters are struggling with the government's policy."},{"de":"Die Trainerin haderte {{mit}} der Entscheidung des Schiedsrichters.","en":"The coach was unhappy with the referee's decision."}]},
 {"w":"liebäugeln","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to toy with the idea of, to have one's eye on","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit liebäugelt sie?","decoys":["für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat."],"ex":[{"de":"Sie liebäugelt schon lange {{mit}} einem Studium im Ausland.","en":"She has been toying with the idea of studying abroad for a long time."},{"de":"Mehrere Fraktionen liebäugeln {{mit}} einer Neuwahl.","en":"Several parliamentary groups are flirting with the idea of a new election."},{"de":"Er liebäugelte {{mit}} dem Gedanken, auszuwandern.","en":"He toyed with the thought of emigrating."}]},
 {"w":"sympathisieren","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to sympathise with, to be sympathetic to","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Mit wem sympathisiert er? / Womit sympathisiert sie?","decoys":["für + Akk.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat.","bei + Dat."],"note":"Often political: mit einer Partei / Bewegung sympathisieren.","ex":[{"de":"Viele Studenten sympathisierten damals {{mit}} den Protesten.","en":"Many students sympathised with the protests at the time."},{"de":"Sie sympathisiert {{mit}} der Idee eines Grundeinkommens.","en":"She is sympathetic to the idea of a basic income."},{"de":"Er wurde verdächtigt, {{mit}} Extremisten zu sympathisieren.","en":"He was suspected of sympathising with extremists."}]},
 {"w":"kollidieren","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to clash with, to collide with","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit kollidiert das? / Mit wem ist er kollidiert?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Perfect with sein for physical collisions (ist kollidiert); in the figurative sense (interests, dates, laws clash) haben is also used (hat kollidiert).","ex":[{"de":"Der Neubau kollidiert {{mit}} den Vorgaben des Denkmalschutzes.","en":"The new building clashes with the heritage-protection requirements."},{"de":"Ihre Termine kollidierten {{mit}} meiner Dienstreise.","en":"Her appointments clashed with my business trip."},{"de":"Ein Lkw ist auf der A8 {{mit}} einem Transporter kollidiert.","en":"A lorry collided with a van on the A8."}]},
 {"w":"sich abfinden","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to come to terms with, to accept","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit findet er sich nicht ab?","decoys":["an + Dat.","über + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Separable. Transitive: jdn. mit Geld abfinden = to pay someone off.","ex":[{"de":"Er konnte sich nicht {{mit}} dem Verlust seines Arbeitsplatzes abfinden.","en":"He could not come to terms with the loss of his job."},{"de":"Die Anwohner haben sich {{mit}} dem Fluglärm abgefunden.","en":"The residents have resigned themselves to the aircraft noise."},{"de":"Man muss sich {{mit}} der neuen Situation abfinden.","en":"One has to accept the new situation."}]},
 {"w":"sich solidarisieren","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to show solidarity with","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Mit wem solidarisieren sich die Studenten?","decoys":["an + Dat.","zu + Dat.","bei + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Hunderte Kollegen solidarisierten sich {{mit}} den Streikenden.","en":"Hundreds of colleagues declared their solidarity with the strikers."},{"de":"Die Opposition solidarisierte sich {{mit}} der verfolgten Journalistin.","en":"The opposition declared its solidarity with the persecuted journalist."},{"de":"Prominente haben sich {{mit}} den Demonstranten solidarisiert.","en":"Celebrities have shown solidarity with the demonstrators."}]},
 {"w":"einhergehen","kind":"v","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"to go hand in hand with, to be accompanied by","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit geht das einher?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","von + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Separable; Bildungssprache. Subject is usually a thing or process, not a person.","ex":[{"de":"Die Digitalisierung geht {{mit}} tiefgreifenden Veränderungen der Arbeitswelt einher.","en":"Digitalisation goes hand in hand with profound changes in the working world."},{"de":"Hohe Gewinne gehen oft {{mit}} hohen Risiken einher.","en":"High profits often go hand in hand with high risks."},{"de":"Die Krankheit geht {{mit}} starken Schmerzen einher.","en":"The illness is accompanied by severe pain."}]},
 {"w":"sich hinwegsetzen","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to disregard, to defy","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber hat er sich hinweggesetzt?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"Separable. Compare hinwegsehen über (to overlook).","ex":[{"de":"Der Präsident setzte sich {{über}} das Urteil des Gerichts hinweg.","en":"The president disregarded the court's ruling."},{"de":"Wer sich {{über}} Verkehrsregeln hinwegsetzt, gefährdet andere.","en":"Anyone who disregards traffic rules endangers others."},{"de":"Sie hat sich {{über}} alle Bedenken hinweggesetzt.","en":"She brushed aside all reservations."}]},
 {"w":"hinwegtäuschen","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to mask, to distract from (a fact)","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber täuscht das hinweg?","decoys":["von + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Separable. The subject is usually a thing: Das täuscht nicht darüber hinweg, dass …","ex":[{"de":"Der Optimismus der Regierung täuscht {{über}} die tatsächliche Lage hinweg.","en":"The government's optimism masks the real situation."},{"de":"Sein Lächeln konnte nicht {{über}} seine Nervosität hinwegtäuschen.","en":"His smile could not hide his nervousness."},{"de":"Die guten Quartalszahlen täuschen nicht {{über}} die strukturellen Probleme hinweg.","en":"The good quarterly figures do not hide the structural problems."}]},
 {"w":"wachen","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to watch over, to ensure compliance with","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber wacht die Behörde? / Über wen wacht sie?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","für + Akk.","um + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Formal: über etwas wachen. At a sickbed one says bei jdm. wachen.","ex":[{"de":"Eine unabhängige Behörde wacht {{über}} die Einhaltung der Datenschutzregeln.","en":"An independent authority ensures that data-protection rules are observed."},{"de":"Die Wölfin wacht {{über}} ihre Jungen.","en":"The she-wolf watches over her cubs."},{"de":"Das Gericht wacht {{über}} die Wahrung der Grundrechte.","en":"The court safeguards the protection of fundamental rights."}]},
 {"w":"befinden","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to decide on, to rule on (formal)","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber befindet das Gericht?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","um + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Amtsdeutsch / legal. Everyday equivalent: entscheiden über.","ex":[{"de":"Der Ausschuss befindet morgen {{über}} den Antrag.","en":"The committee will decide on the motion tomorrow."},{"de":"Das Parlament soll {{über}} die Verlängerung des Mandats befinden.","en":"Parliament is to decide on the extension of the mandate."},{"de":"Allein das Gericht befindet {{über}} die Zulassung der Klage.","en":"Only the court decides on the admissibility of the lawsuit."}]},
 {"w":"zurückschrecken","kind":"v","prep":"vor","case":"Dat","en":"to shrink from, to shy away from","lv":"C1","da":"davor","wo":"Wovor schreckt er zurück? / Vor wem schreckt er zurück?","decoys":["von + Dat.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Separable. Typical: vor nichts zurückschrecken.","ex":[{"de":"Die Täter schreckten auch {{vor}} Gewalt nicht zurück.","en":"The perpetrators did not shrink from violence either."},{"de":"Er schreckt nicht {{vor}} unpopulären Entscheidungen zurück.","en":"He does not shy away from unpopular decisions."},{"de":"Viele Anleger schrecken {{vor}} dem hohen Risiko zurück.","en":"Many investors shy away from the high risk."}]},
 {"w":"kapitulieren","kind":"v","prep":"vor","case":"Dat","en":"to surrender to, to give in to","lv":"C1","da":"davor","wo":"Wovor kapituliert er? / Vor wem kapituliert die Armee?","decoys":["gegen + Akk.","an + Dat.","von + Dat.","für + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Die Armee kapitulierte schließlich {{vor}} der Übermacht des Feindes.","en":"The army finally surrendered to the enemy's superior force."},{"de":"Die Regierung will nicht {{vor}} den Forderungen der Erpresser kapitulieren.","en":"The government will not give in to the blackmailers' demands."},{"de":"Man darf nicht {{vor}} jeder Schwierigkeit kapitulieren.","en":"One must not give up in the face of every difficulty."}]},
 {"w":"spekulieren","kind":"v","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"to count on, to bank on","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf spekuliert er?","decoys":["für + Akk.","zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Meaning depends on the preposition: spekulieren auf (count on), spekulieren mit (trade in), spekulieren über (conjecture about).","ex":[{"de":"Viele Anleger spekulieren {{auf}} steigende Kurse.","en":"Many investors are betting on rising prices."},{"de":"Sie spekuliert {{auf}} einen Posten in der Geschäftsleitung.","en":"She is hoping for a position in senior management."},{"de":"Der Verein spekuliert {{auf}} den Aufstieg in die erste Liga.","en":"The club is banking on promotion to the first division."}],"sense":"to count on"},
 {"w":"trachten","kind":"v","prep":"nach","case":"Dat","en":"to strive for, to seek (formal, often negative)","lv":"C1","da":"danach","wo":"Wonach trachtet er?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","für + Akk.","zu + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Literary/formal. Idiom: jdm. nach dem Leben trachten (to try to kill someone). Compare streben nach.","ex":[{"de":"Er trachtete sein Leben lang {{nach}} Macht und Einfluss.","en":"All his life he sought power and influence."},{"de":"Die Verschwörer trachteten dem König {{nach}} dem Leben.","en":"The conspirators sought the king's life."},{"de":"Wer {{nach}} Ruhm trachtet, muss Opfer bringen.","en":"Anyone who strives for fame has to make sacrifices."}]},
 {"w":"sich auflehnen","kind":"v","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"to rebel against, to revolt against","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen lehnen sie sich auf? / Gegen wen lehnt er sich auf?","decoys":["um + Akk.","an + Akk.","über + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Separable: sich gegen etwas auflehnen.","ex":[{"de":"Die Bevölkerung lehnte sich {{gegen}} die Willkür der Behörden auf.","en":"The population rebelled against the arbitrary rule of the authorities."},{"de":"Jugendliche lehnen sich oft {{gegen}} die Autorität der Eltern auf.","en":"Teenagers often rebel against their parents' authority."},{"de":"Er wagte es nicht, sich offen {{gegen}} den Vorstand aufzulehnen.","en":"He did not dare to rebel openly against the board."}]},
 {"w":"sich sträuben","kind":"v","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"to resist, to balk at","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen sträubt er sich?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","vor + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"Idiom: Mir sträuben sich die Haare. (My hair stands on end.)","ex":[{"de":"Die Opposition sträubt sich {{gegen}} eine Verlängerung der Frist.","en":"The opposition is resisting an extension of the deadline."},{"de":"Er sträubte sich lange {{gegen}} die Anschaffung eines neuen Computers.","en":"For a long time he resisted buying a new computer."},{"de":"Viele Länder sträuben sich {{gegen}} verbindliche Klimaziele.","en":"Many countries are balking at binding climate targets."}]},
 {"w":"sich klammern","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"to cling to","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran klammert sie sich? / An wen klammert er sich?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Literal and figurative. Akk. (movement towards the thing grasped).","ex":[{"de":"Die Überlebenden klammerten sich {{an}} Wrackteile.","en":"The survivors clung to pieces of wreckage."},{"de":"Er klammert sich {{an}} die Hoffnung, dass alles gut wird.","en":"He clings to the hope that everything will turn out well."},{"de":"Die Regierung klammert sich {{an}} ihre Macht.","en":"The government is clinging to its power."}]},
 {"w":"mangeln","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"to lack, to be short of (impersonal)","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran mangelt es?","decoys":["für + Akk.","von + Dat.","mit + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Mostly impersonal: es mangelt (jdm.) an etwas = es fehlt an etwas.","ex":[{"de":"Den Behörden mangelt es {{an}} Personal.","en":"The authorities are short of staff."},{"de":"Es mangelt dem Land {{an}} Fachkräften.","en":"The country lacks skilled workers."},{"de":"Es mangelt {{an}} klaren Zuständigkeiten.","en":"There is a lack of clear responsibilities."}]},
 {"w":"kranken","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"to suffer from (a flaw)","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran krankt das System?","decoys":["von + Dat.","unter + Dat.","mit + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Figurative, about systems and plans. Illness of persons: leiden an / erkranken an.","ex":[{"de":"Das Gesundheitssystem krankt {{an}} chronischer Unterfinanzierung.","en":"The healthcare system suffers from chronic underfunding."},{"de":"Der Plan krankt {{an}} einem grundlegenden Denkfehler.","en":"The plan suffers from a fundamental logical flaw."},{"de":"Die Reform krankt {{an}} mangelnder Akzeptanz.","en":"The reform suffers from a lack of acceptance."}]},
 {"w":"schöpfen","kind":"v","prep":"aus","case":"Dat","en":"to draw (strength, hope) from","lv":"C1","da":"daraus","wo":"Woraus schöpft sie Kraft?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","um + Akk.","nach + Dat."],"note":"Fixed: Mut / Kraft / Hoffnung schöpfen aus etwas.","ex":[{"de":"Sie schöpft Kraft {{aus}} ihrem Glauben.","en":"She draws strength from her faith."},{"de":"Die Autorin schöpft {{aus}} einem reichen Erfahrungsschatz.","en":"The author draws on a rich store of experience."},{"de":"Nach der Niederlage schöpften sie neuen Mut {{aus}} dem Zuspruch der Fans.","en":"After the defeat they drew new courage from the fans' encouragement."}]},
 {"w":"bürgen","kind":"v","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"to vouch for, to guarantee","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür bürgt er? / Für wen bürgt sie?","decoys":["an + Akk.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Financial (guarantor) and figurative (guarantee of quality).","ex":[{"de":"Die Eltern bürgen {{für}} den Kredit ihrer Tochter.","en":"The parents stand surety for their daughter's loan."},{"de":"Der Name der Firma bürgt {{für}} Qualität.","en":"The company's name is a guarantee of quality."},{"de":"Ich bürge persönlich {{für}} ihn.","en":"I personally vouch for him."}]},
 {"w":"aufkommen","kind":"v","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"to bear the cost of, to be liable for","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür kommt die Versicherung auf?","decoys":["an + Akk.","über + Akk.","um + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Separable: für etwas aufkommen. Other meaning: gegen jdn. aufkommen (to prevail against).","ex":[{"de":"Der Verursacher muss {{für}} den Schaden aufkommen.","en":"The party responsible must pay for the damage."},{"de":"Die Versicherung kommt nicht {{für}} Vorerkrankungen auf.","en":"The insurance does not cover pre-existing conditions."},{"de":"Wer kommt {{für}} die Kosten der Sanierung auf?","en":"Who will bear the costs of the renovation?"}],"sense":"to bear the cost of"},
 {"w":"ringen","kind":"v","prep":"um","case":"Akk","en":"to struggle for, to fight for","lv":"C1","da":"darum","wo":"Worum ringen sie?","decoys":["über + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Other prepositions, other meanings: nach Luft ringen (gasp for air), mit jdm. ringen (wrestle).","ex":[{"de":"Die Verhandlungspartner ringen seit Wochen {{um}} eine Lösung.","en":"The negotiating parties have been struggling for a solution for weeks."},{"de":"Die beiden Athletinnen rangen bis zuletzt {{um}} den Sieg.","en":"The two athletes fought for victory until the very end."},{"de":"Die Gewerkschaft ringt {{um}} jeden Arbeitsplatz.","en":"The union is fighting for every single job."}]},
 {"w":"bestärken","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"to reinforce (in a belief), to encourage in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin bestärkt ihn das?","decoys":["in + Akk.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"jdn. in etwas bestärken: the thing is in the Dat. (in seiner Meinung).","ex":[{"de":"Der Erfolg bestärkte ihn {{in}} seiner Überzeugung.","en":"The success reinforced his conviction."},{"de":"Die Lehrerin bestärkte die Schüler {{in}} ihrem Vorhaben.","en":"The teacher encouraged the pupils in their plan."},{"de":"Diese Zahlen bestärken uns {{in}} unserer Skepsis.","en":"These figures reinforce our scepticism."}]},
 {"w":"sich auslassen","kind":"v","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"to hold forth about, to expound on","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber lässt er sich aus?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","von + Dat.","an + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Separable; slightly negative (to go on at length). Neutral: sich äußern zu.","ex":[{"de":"Der Minister ließ sich ausführlich {{über}} die Vorzüge des Projekts aus.","en":"The minister held forth at length about the merits of the project."},{"de":"Sie ließ sich {{über}} die Fehler ihrer Kollegen aus.","en":"She spoke at length about her colleagues' mistakes."},{"de":"Er lässt sich gern {{über}} seine Reisen aus.","en":"He likes to go on about his travels."}]},
 {"w":"sich bekennen","kind":"v","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"to profess, to acknowledge (publicly)","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu bekennt er sich?","decoys":["an + Akk.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Formal. Also: sich schuldig bekennen (reflexive + adjective, no preposition).","ex":[{"de":"Die Regierung bekennt sich {{zu}} ihrer historischen Verantwortung.","en":"The government acknowledges its historical responsibility."},{"de":"Der Täter bekannte sich {{zu}} dem Anschlag.","en":"The perpetrator claimed responsibility for the attack."},{"de":"Viele Unternehmen bekennen sich {{zu}} mehr Klimaschutz.","en":"Many companies publicly commit to more climate protection."}]},
 {"w":"berechtigen","kind":"v","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"to entitle to, to justify","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu berechtigt dieser Ausweis?","decoys":["für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk."],"note":"Legal/formal; often passive: berechtigt sein zu. Subject is a thing (Ausweis, Vollmacht, Erfolg).","ex":[{"de":"Der Ausweis berechtigt {{zu}} freiem Eintritt in alle Museen.","en":"The pass entitles the holder to free admission to all museums."},{"de":"Diese Zahlen berechtigen {{zu}} der Hoffnung, dass sich die Lage bessert.","en":"These figures justify the hope that the situation is improving."},{"de":"Die Vollmacht berechtigt ihn {{zu}} Abhebungen vom Konto.","en":"The power of attorney entitles him to make withdrawals from the account."}]},
 {"w":"sich entzünden","kind":"v","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"to flare up over, to be sparked by","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran hat sich der Streit entzündet?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","mit + Dat.","auf + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Figurative (conflicts, debates, protests). Literal: etwas entzündet sich (catches fire).","ex":[{"de":"Der Streit entzündete sich {{an}} einer Kleinigkeit.","en":"The quarrel flared up over a trifle."},{"de":"Die Proteste entzündeten sich {{an}} der Erhöhung der Fahrpreise.","en":"The protests were sparked by the increase in fares."},{"de":"Die Debatte hatte sich {{an}} einem unbedachten Satz des Ministers entzündet.","en":"The debate had been sparked by a careless remark by the minister."}]},
 {"w":"ausarten","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to degenerate into, to turn into (something bad)","lv":"C1","da":"darin (v. a. mit dass-Satz: Es artete darin aus, dass …)","wo":"In was ist der Streit ausgeartet? (ugs.)","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","um + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Separable: artet aus. Always negative: in Streit / Gewalt / Arbeit / Stress ausarten.","ex":[{"de":"Die Diskussion artete {{in}} einen offenen Streit aus.","en":"The discussion degenerated into an open quarrel."},{"de":"Die Party ist völlig {{in}} eine Schlägerei ausgeartet.","en":"The party degenerated completely into a brawl."},{"de":"Der Ausflug droht {{in}} Stress auszuarten.","en":"The outing threatens to turn into a stressful ordeal."}]},
 {"w":"umschlagen","kind":"v","prep":"in","case":"Akk","en":"to turn into, to change abruptly into","lv":"C1","da":"– (kein gebräuchliches da-Wort)","wo":"In was ist die Stimmung umgeschlagen?","decoys":["für + Akk.","um + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Separable. Perfect with sein: ist umgeschlagen. Sudden change of a state or mood.","ex":[{"de":"Die Begeisterung schlug plötzlich {{in}} Wut um.","en":"The enthusiasm suddenly turned into anger."},{"de":"Das Wetter schlägt am Abend {{in}} Regen um.","en":"The weather turns to rain in the evening."},{"de":"Die Stimmung im Land ist {{in}} Misstrauen umgeschlagen.","en":"The mood in the country has turned to mistrust."}]},
 {"w":"beipflichten","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to agree with, to concur with","lv":"C1","note":"Separable: pflichtet … bei. Formal; ≈ zustimmen.","ex":[{"de":"Der Redner pflichtete seinem Vorgänger in diesem Punkt bei.","en":"The speaker concurred with his predecessor on this point."},{"de":"Ich muss dir da leider beipflichten.","en":"I'm afraid I have to agree with you there."},{"de":"Alle Anwesenden pflichteten der Kritik bei.","en":"All those present agreed with the criticism."}]},
 {"w":"zuwiderhandeln","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to contravene, to act in breach of","lv":"C1","note":"Separable, legal register: handelt … zuwider. Past participle: zuwidergehandelt.","ex":[{"de":"Wer dem Verbot zuwiderhandelt, wird mit einer Geldstrafe belegt.","en":"Anyone who contravenes the ban will be fined."},{"de":"Er hat den Anweisungen seines Vorgesetzten zuwidergehandelt.","en":"He acted against his superior's instructions."},{"de":"Mitarbeiter, die dieser Vorschrift zuwiderhandeln, müssen mit Konsequenzen rechnen.","en":"Employees who violate this regulation must expect consequences."}]},
 {"w":"zuwiderlaufen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to run counter to, to be contrary to","lv":"C1","note":"Separable: läuft … zuwider. Subject is a thing (Plan, Maßnahme, Entscheidung).","ex":[{"de":"Dieser Plan läuft den Interessen der Anwohner zuwider.","en":"This plan runs counter to the residents' interests."},{"de":"Solche Maßnahmen würden dem Geist des Gesetzes zuwiderlaufen.","en":"Such measures would run counter to the spirit of the law."},{"de":"Die Entscheidung lief jeder Vernunft zuwider.","en":"The decision was contrary to all reason."}]},
 {"w":"obliegen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to be the responsibility of, to fall to","lv":"C1","note":"Formal; used almost only in the third person: Die Pflicht obliegt jdm. / Es obliegt jdm., zu …","ex":[{"de":"Die Aufsicht obliegt dem Vorstand.","en":"Supervision is the board's responsibility."},{"de":"Es obliegt dem Arbeitgeber, für sichere Arbeitsplätze zu sorgen.","en":"It is the employer's duty to provide safe workplaces."},{"de":"Die Entscheidung obliegt allein den Eltern.","en":"The decision rests solely with the parents."}]},
 {"w":"widerfahren","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to happen to, to befall","lv":"C1","note":"Literary/formal; perfect with sein: ist widerfahren. Fixed: jdm. Gerechtigkeit widerfahren lassen.","ex":[{"de":"Dem Opfer ist großes Unrecht widerfahren.","en":"Great injustice befell the victim."},{"de":"Ihm widerfuhr eine unerwartete Ehre.","en":"An unexpected honour came his way."},{"de":"Was ist dir denn widerfahren?","en":"What on earth happened to you?"}]},
 {"w":"gebühren","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to be due to, to deserve","lv":"C1","note":"Formal: Dank, Respekt, Anerkennung gebührt jdm. Also reflexive: wie es sich gebührt.","ex":[{"de":"Dem Sieger gebührt der Preis.","en":"The prize is due to the winner."},{"de":"Ihr gebührt unser aufrichtiger Dank.","en":"She deserves our sincere thanks."},{"de":"Den Pflegekräften gebührt mehr Anerkennung für ihre Arbeit.","en":"Nursing staff deserve more recognition for their work."}]},
 {"w":"frönen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to indulge in, to give oneself over to","lv":"C1","note":"Literary or ironic; usually of a vice or great passion.","ex":[{"de":"Er frönt seit Jahren dem Glücksspiel.","en":"He has been indulging in gambling for years."},{"de":"Im Urlaub frönen wir dem Müßiggang.","en":"On holiday we give ourselves over to idleness."},{"de":"Sie frönte ihrer Leidenschaft für alte Bücher.","en":"She indulged her passion for old books."}]},
 {"w":"huldigen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to pay homage to, to subscribe to","lv":"C1","note":"Formal or ironic. With ideas: einem Prinzip / einer Idee huldigen.","ex":[{"de":"Die Dichter huldigten dem Herrscher in Oden.","en":"The poets paid homage to the ruler in odes."},{"de":"Er huldigt dem Grundsatz, dass Sparsamkeit eine Tugend sei.","en":"He subscribes to the principle that thrift is a virtue."},{"de":"Die Branche huldigt noch immer dem Mythos vom genialen Einzelgänger.","en":"The industry still pays homage to the myth of the lone genius."}]},
 {"w":"abhelfen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to remedy, to put right","lv":"C1","note":"Separable: hilft … ab. Formal; often passive: Dem wird abgeholfen.","ex":[{"de":"Die Stadt will dem Wohnungsmangel durch Neubauten abhelfen.","en":"The city wants to remedy the housing shortage by building new homes."},{"de":"Diesem Missstand muss dringend abgeholfen werden.","en":"This deplorable state of affairs must be remedied urgently."},{"de":"Wie kann man diesem Problem abhelfen?","en":"How can this problem be remedied?"}]},
 {"w":"beikommen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to get the better of, to get to grips with","lv":"C1","note":"Separable (beizukommen); mostly negated or with schwer. Often impersonal passive: Dem ist nicht beizukommen.","ex":[{"de":"Dem Problem ist mit Geld allein nicht beizukommen.","en":"The problem cannot be solved with money alone."},{"de":"Einem solchen Betrugsring ist schwer beizukommen.","en":"Such a fraud ring is hard to get at."},{"de":"Seiner Sturheit kommt man kaum bei.","en":"One can hardly get the better of his stubbornness."}]},
 {"w":"beiwohnen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to attend, to be present at (formal)","lv":"C1","note":"Separable: wohnt … bei. Very formal; everyday: teilnehmen an / dabei sein.","ex":[{"de":"Der Präsident wohnte der Feier bei.","en":"The president attended the ceremony."},{"de":"Mehrere Journalisten durften der Verhandlung beiwohnen.","en":"Several journalists were allowed to be present at the hearing."},{"de":"Ich hatte die Ehre, der Zeremonie beizuwohnen.","en":"I had the honour of attending the ceremony."}]},
 {"w":"verfallen","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to fall prey to, to become addicted to","lv":"C1","sense":"to fall prey to","note":"Perfect with sein: ist verfallen. Not to be confused with verfallen in + Akk. (in Schweigen verfallen) or verfallen auf (to hit upon an idea).","ex":[{"de":"Er ist dem Alkohol verfallen.","en":"He has fallen prey to alcohol."},{"de":"Viele junge Menschen verfallen dem Glücksspiel.","en":"Many young people fall prey to gambling."},{"de":"Sie war dem Charme des Fremden völlig verfallen.","en":"She had completely fallen for the stranger's charm."}]},
 {"w":"sich verschreiben (Sache)","kind":"c","case":"Dat","en":"to devote oneself to, to dedicate oneself to","lv":"C1","sense":"to devote oneself to","note":"sich (Akk.) einer Sache (Dat.) verschreiben. (Another meaning: etwas verschreiben = to prescribe.)","ex":[{"de":"Die Stiftung hat sich dem Naturschutz verschrieben.","en":"The foundation has dedicated itself to nature conservation."},{"de":"Er verschrieb sich ganz der Wissenschaft.","en":"He devoted himself entirely to science."},{"de":"Das Restaurant hat sich der regionalen Küche verschrieben.","en":"The restaurant is dedicated to regional cuisine."}]},
 {"w":"bezichtigen (Tat)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to accuse of, to charge with","lv":"C1","note":"jdn. einer Sache bezichtigen; formal. Compare beschuldigen (also + Gen.). The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Man bezichtigte ihn der Lüge.","en":"They accused him of lying."},{"de":"Die Zeitung bezichtigte den Minister der Korruption.","en":"The newspaper accused the minister of corruption."},{"de":"Sie bezichtigte sich selbst des Verrats.","en":"She accused herself of betrayal."}]},
 {"w":"überführen (Tat)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to prove guilty of, to convict of (by evidence)","lv":"C1","sense":"to convict","note":"jdn. einer Tat überführen. Another meaning: etwas/jdn. überführen (Akk.) = to transfer, e.g. in ein anderes Krankenhaus. The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Der Täter wurde durch DNA-Spuren des Mordes überführt.","en":"DNA traces proved the perpetrator guilty of the murder."},{"de":"Es gelang der Polizei, die Bande des Betrugs zu überführen.","en":"The police managed to prove the gang guilty of fraud."},{"de":"Man konnte ihn der Lüge überführen.","en":"He could be shown to have lied."}]},
 {"w":"verdächtigen (Tat)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to suspect of","lv":"C1","note":"jdn. einer Sache verdächtigen: the offence is in the Gen. The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Man verdächtigt ihn des Diebstahls.","en":"He is suspected of theft."},{"de":"Sie wurde der Spionage verdächtigt.","en":"She was suspected of espionage."},{"de":"Die Polizei verdächtigte ihn eines Raubüberfalls.","en":"The police suspected him of a robbery."}]},
 {"w":"anklagen (Tat)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to charge with, to indict for","lv":"C1","note":"Separable: klagt … an. jdn. einer Tat anklagen; alternatively wegen + Gen. (wegen Mordes). The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Er wurde des Mordes angeklagt.","en":"He was charged with murder."},{"de":"Die Staatsanwaltschaft klagt den Geschäftsführer der Untreue an.","en":"The public prosecutor is charging the managing director with breach of trust."},{"de":"Sie wurden des Betrugs angeklagt.","en":"They were charged with fraud."}]},
 {"w":"sich versichern","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to make sure of, to secure","lv":"C1","sense":"to make sure of","note":"sich einer Sache versichern (formal). Not to be confused with sich gegen etwas versichern (to take out insurance). Reflexive pronoun accusative; the object is genitive.","ex":[{"de":"Der Konzern wollte sich der Unterstützung der Banken versichern.","en":"The group wanted to make sure of the banks' support."},{"de":"Bevor er losfuhr, versicherte er sich der Zustimmung seiner Frau.","en":"Before setting off he made sure of his wife's approval."},{"de":"Sie versicherte sich seiner Loyalität.","en":"She made sure of his loyalty."}]},
 {"w":"sich erwehren","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to fend off, to resist","lv":"C1","note":"Literary/formal; mostly in the fixed phrase sich des Eindrucks nicht erwehren können. Reflexive pronoun accusative; the object is genitive.","ex":[{"de":"Die Verteidiger erwehrten sich des Angriffs nur mit Mühe.","en":"The defenders only just fended off the attack."},{"de":"Man kann sich des Eindrucks nicht erwehren, dass hier etwas verschwiegen wird.","en":"One cannot help feeling that something is being concealed here."},{"de":"Er konnte sich der Vorwürfe kaum erwehren.","en":"He could hardly fend off the accusations."}]},
 {"w":"berauben (Sache)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to rob of, to deprive of","lv":"C1","note":"jdn. einer Sache berauben (Gen.); formal/literary. The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Der Krieg beraubte viele Familien ihrer Heimat.","en":"The war deprived many families of their homeland."},{"de":"Die Diktatur beraubte die Bürger ihrer Freiheit.","en":"The dictatorship robbed the citizens of their freedom."},{"de":"Der Unfall hat ihn seiner Lebensfreude beraubt.","en":"The accident robbed him of his joy in life."}]},
 {"w":"entheben (Amt)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to relieve of, to dismiss from","lv":"C1","note":"jdn. einer Sache entheben; often passive: seines Amtes enthoben werden. The person is accusative; the question is the case of the second object.","ex":[{"de":"Der Präsident enthob den Minister seines Amtes.","en":"The president removed the minister from office."},{"de":"Der Beamte wurde seines Dienstes enthoben.","en":"The civil servant was relieved of his duties."},{"de":"Der Trainer wurde mit sofortiger Wirkung seiner Aufgaben enthoben.","en":"The coach was relieved of his duties with immediate effect."}]},
 {"w":"entbehren (= ohne etw. sein)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to lack, to be devoid of","lv":"C1","sense":"to lack","note":"Formal; Gen. object, typically with jeder / nicht. Different meaning with Akk.: etwas nicht entbehren können (to be unable to do without).","ex":[{"de":"Diese Behauptung entbehrt jeder Grundlage.","en":"This claim has no basis whatsoever."},{"de":"Seine Rede entbehrte nicht eines gewissen Humors.","en":"His speech was not without a certain humour."},{"de":"Die Geschichte entbehrt jeder Wahrscheinlichkeit.","en":"The story lacks all plausibility."}]},
 {"w":"würdigen (Blick, Wort)","kind":"c","case":"Gen","en":"to deign to give (fixed with negation)","lv":"C1","sense":"to deign to give","note":"Only in fixed uses such as jdn. keines Blickes / keines Wortes / keiner Erwähnung würdigen. Otherwise würdigen takes Akk. (to appreciate). The person is accusative; Blick/Wort is genitive.","ex":[{"de":"Er würdigte mich keines Blickes.","en":"He did not deign to look at me."},{"de":"Die Zeitung würdigte den Vorfall keiner Erwähnung.","en":"The newspaper did not deign to mention the incident."},{"de":"Sie würdigte ihn keines Wortes.","en":"She did not deign to say a word to him."}]},
 {"w":"der Hinweis","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"indication of, pointer to, reference to","lv":"B2","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf gibt es einen Hinweis? / Auf wen gibt es einen Hinweis?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","nach + Dat.","um + Akk.","zu + Akk."],"note":"Related: hinweisen auf; ein Hinweis darauf, dass …","ex":[{"de":"Es gibt keinen Hinweis {{auf}} einen Einbruch.","en":"There is no indication of a break-in."},{"de":"Der Hinweis {{auf}} die Frist stand nur im Kleingedruckten.","en":"The note about the deadline was only in the small print."},{"de":"Die Polizei bittet um Hinweise {{auf}} den Täter.","en":"The police are asking for tips about the culprit."}]},
 {"w":"der Verdacht","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"suspicion of (a suspected offence, illness, …)","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf besteht der Verdacht? / Auf wen fällt der Verdacht?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","an + Akk.","über + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Typical (esp. medical): der Verdacht auf Krebs / auf eine Infektion. Legal language often uses the genitive: der Verdacht des Betrugs. Against a person: der Verdacht gegen jemanden.","ex":[{"de":"Bei dem Patienten besteht der Verdacht {{auf}} eine Lungenentzündung.","en":"The patient is suspected of having pneumonia."},{"de":"Wegen des Verdachts {{auf}} Salmonellen ruft der Hersteller den Käse zurück.","en":"The manufacturer is recalling the cheese on suspicion of salmonella."},{"de":"Der Verdacht fiel schnell {{auf}} den Nachbarn.","en":"Suspicion quickly fell on the neighbour."}]},
 {"w":"der Rückschluss","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"inference about, conclusion regarding","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf lässt das Rückschlüsse zu? / Auf wen lassen die Spuren Rückschlüsse zu?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","an + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","nach + Dat."],"note":"Rückschlüsse ziehen aus (the evidence) auf (the conclusion); also: ein Rückschluss von A auf B.","ex":[{"de":"Die Daten lassen keinen Rückschluss {{auf}} die Ursache zu.","en":"The data do not allow any conclusion about the cause."},{"de":"Aus dem Dialekt zog er Rückschlüsse {{auf}} ihre Herkunft.","en":"From her dialect he drew inferences about her origin."},{"de":"Ein Rückschluss {{auf}} den Täter ist anhand der Spuren nicht möglich.","en":"No inference about the culprit is possible from the traces."}]},
 {"w":"der Zusammenhang","kind":"n","prep":"zwischen","case":"Dat","en":"connection between","lv":"B2","da":"zwischen ihnen (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Zwischen wem / was besteht ein Zusammenhang? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zwischen + Akk.","über + Akk.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Zusammenhang mit = link with one thing; Zusammenhang zwischen needs two things (A und B). Here zwischen takes the dative (no movement).","ex":[{"de":"Es gibt einen klaren Zusammenhang {{zwischen}} Schlafmangel und Konzentrationsproblemen.","en":"There is a clear connection between lack of sleep and concentration problems."},{"de":"Die Forscher untersuchen den Zusammenhang {{zwischen}} den beiden Phänomenen.","en":"The researchers are investigating the connection between the two phenomena."},{"de":"Einen Zusammenhang {{zwischen}} diesen Vorfällen konnte die Polizei nicht herstellen.","en":"The police could not establish a connection between these incidents."}],"alt":["von + Dat."]},
 {"w":"die Kluft","kind":"n","prep":"zwischen","case":"Dat","en":"gap, rift between","lv":"C1","da":"zwischen ihnen (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Zwischen wem / was besteht eine Kluft? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zwischen + Akk.","über + Akk.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Die Kluft {{zwischen}} Arm und Reich wird immer größer.","en":"The gap between rich and poor keeps growing."},{"de":"Eine tiefe Kluft {{zwischen}} den Generationen prägt die Debatte.","en":"A deep rift between the generations shapes the debate."},{"de":"Er versuchte, die Kluft {{zwischen}} den beiden Lagern zu überbrücken.","en":"He tried to bridge the gap between the two camps."}]},
 {"w":"die Beteiligung","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"participation in, involvement in; stake in","lv":"B2","da":"daran","wo":"Woran hat die Firma eine Beteiligung erworben? / An welchem Unternehmen hat er eine Beteiligung?","decoys":["an + Akk.","auf + Akk.","in + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Also in the financial sense: eine Beteiligung an einem Unternehmen (a stake).","ex":[{"de":"Ihre Beteiligung {{an}} diesem Projekt war entscheidend.","en":"Her involvement in this project was decisive."},{"de":"Die Firma hat eine Beteiligung {{an}} einem Start-up erworben.","en":"The company has acquired a stake in a start-up."},{"de":"Man wirft ihm die Beteiligung {{an}} einem Betrug vor.","en":"He is accused of involvement in a fraud."}]},
 {"w":"die Zuständigkeit","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"responsibility, jurisdiction for","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür hat das Amt die Zuständigkeit? / Für wen ist das Amt zuständig?","decoys":["an + Akk.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"Official/administrative language; the adjective is zuständig für.","ex":[{"de":"Die Zuständigkeit {{für}} Passangelegenheiten liegt beim Bürgeramt.","en":"The citizens' office is responsible for passport matters."},{"de":"Das Gericht verneinte seine Zuständigkeit {{für}} den Fall.","en":"The court denied that it had jurisdiction over the case."},{"de":"Unklare Zuständigkeiten {{für}} die Schulsanierung führten zu Verzögerungen.","en":"Unclear responsibilities for the school renovation led to delays."}]},
 {"w":"die Voraussetzung","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"prerequisite for, precondition for","lv":"B2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das eine Voraussetzung?","decoys":["über + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Also: die Voraussetzung dafür, dass …; unter der Voraussetzung, dass … (provided that).","ex":[{"de":"Ein gültiger Pass ist die Voraussetzung {{für}} die Einreise.","en":"A valid passport is the prerequisite for entry."},{"de":"Die Voraussetzungen {{für}} eine Förderung sind streng geregelt.","en":"The requirements for funding are strictly regulated."},{"de":"Gegenseitiges Vertrauen ist eine wichtige Voraussetzung {{für}} jede Partnerschaft.","en":"Mutual trust is an important precondition for any partnership."}]},
 {"w":"die Abkehr","kind":"n","prep":"von","case":"Dat","en":"turning away from, abandonment of","lv":"C1","da":"davon","wo":"Wovon kehrt man sich ab? / Von wem kehrt man sich ab?","decoys":["von + Akk.","zu + Dat.","aus + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Opposite: die Hinwendung zu. Verb: sich abkehren / sich abwenden von.","ex":[{"de":"Die Abkehr {{von}} fossilen Energien soll bis 2040 gelingen.","en":"The move away from fossil fuels is meant to succeed by 2040."},{"de":"Seine Abkehr {{von}} der Partei überraschte alle.","en":"His break with the party surprised everyone."},{"de":"Viele fordern eine Abkehr {{von}} dieser Politik.","en":"Many are demanding a departure from this policy."}]},
 {"w":"die Hinwendung","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"turn towards, shift towards","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu wendet man sich hin? / Zu wem wendet man sich hin?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","auf + Akk.","für + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Opposite: die Abkehr von. Verb: sich hinwenden zu.","ex":[{"de":"Die Hinwendung {{zu}} erneuerbaren Energien beschleunigt sich.","en":"The shift towards renewable energy is speeding up."},{"de":"In seinen späten Jahren erlebte er eine Hinwendung {{zu}} religiösen Fragen.","en":"In his later years he experienced a turn towards religious questions."},{"de":"Die Hinwendung der Firma {{zu}} jüngeren Kunden zahlte sich aus.","en":"The company's turn towards younger customers paid off."}]},
 {"w":"die Anpassung","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"adaptation to, adjustment to","lv":"B2","da":"daran","wo":"Woran wird etwas angepasst? / An wen passt man sich an?","decoys":["an + Dat.","mit + Dat.","vor + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"ex":[{"de":"Die Anpassung {{an}} den Klimawandel kostet viel Geld.","en":"Adapting to climate change costs a lot of money."},{"de":"Die Anpassung der Lehrpläne {{an}} neue Anforderungen dauert Jahre.","en":"Adapting the curricula to new requirements takes years."},{"de":"Ihre schnelle Anpassung {{an}} das neue Umfeld beeindruckte die Lehrer.","en":"Her quick adjustment to the new surroundings impressed the teachers."}]},
 {"w":"die Auseinandersetzung","kind":"n","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"engagement with; confrontation with","lv":"B2","da":"damit","wo":"Womit setzt man sich auseinander? / Mit wem gab es eine Auseinandersetzung?","decoys":["mit + Akk.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"A dispute over something is 'um': die Auseinandersetzung um die Macht.","ex":[{"de":"Die Auseinandersetzung {{mit}} der eigenen Geschichte fiel dem Land schwer.","en":"Coming to terms with its own history was hard for the country."},{"de":"Der Film lädt zu einer kritischen Auseinandersetzung {{mit}} dem Thema ein.","en":"The film invites critical engagement with the subject."},{"de":"Es kam zu einer handfesten Auseinandersetzung {{mit}} den Nachbarn.","en":"There was a physical altercation with the neighbours."}]},
 {"w":"der Bezug","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"reference to (Bezug nehmen auf, in Bezug auf)","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf nimmt sie Bezug? / Auf wen nimmt sie Bezug?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","an + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","nach + Dat."],"note":"Formal: Bezug nehmen auf / in Bezug auf / unter Bezug auf. Not the same as 'einen Bezug zu etwas haben' (a personal connection).","ex":[{"de":"In ihrer Rede nahm sie Bezug {{auf}} die Ereignisse des Vorjahres.","en":"In her speech she referred to the events of the previous year."},{"de":"Unter Bezug {{auf}} Ihr Schreiben vom 3. Mai teilen wir Ihnen mit, dass die Lieferung verspätet ist.","en":"With reference to your letter of 3 May, we inform you that the delivery is delayed."},{"de":"In Bezug {{auf}} die Kosten gibt es noch offene Fragen.","en":"With regard to the costs there are still open questions."}]},
 {"w":"die Verpflichtung","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"obligation to, commitment to","lv":"B2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu besteht eine Verpflichtung?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Dat.","um + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"note":"What you are obliged to do: Verpflichtung zu. Towards whom: Verpflichtung gegenüber.","ex":[{"de":"Die Verpflichtung {{zu}} strikter Verschwiegenheit gilt auch nach dem Vertragsende.","en":"The obligation to strict confidentiality also applies after the contract ends."},{"de":"Der Vertrag enthält die Verpflichtung {{zu}} regelmäßigen Zahlungen.","en":"The contract contains an obligation to make regular payments."},{"de":"Aus dem Gesetz ergibt sich eine Verpflichtung {{zu}} schnellem Handeln.","en":"The law creates an obligation to act quickly."}]},
 {"w":"die Verpflichtung","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"obligation towards (a person or group)","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber besteht die Verpflichtung? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["an + Dat.","mit + Dat.","um + Akk.","in + Akk."],"sense":"towards someone","note":"Towards whom: gegenüber + Dat. What you must do: Verpflichtung zu.","ex":[{"de":"Als Vater hat er eine Verpflichtung {{gegenüber}} seinen Kindern.","en":"As a father he has an obligation towards his children."},{"de":"Die Bank erfüllte ihre Verpflichtung {{gegenüber}} den Anlegern nicht.","en":"The bank did not meet its obligation towards the investors."},{"de":"Wir haben eine moralische Verpflichtung {{gegenüber}} künftigen Generationen.","en":"We have a moral obligation towards future generations."}]},
 {"w":"der Verstoß","kind":"n","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"violation of, breach of","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen hat er verstoßen? / Gegen welche Regel war das ein Verstoß?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","über + Akk."],"note":"Verb: verstoßen gegen. Typical in legal and official language.","ex":[{"de":"Der Verstoß {{gegen}} die Hausordnung wird mit einer Abmahnung geahndet.","en":"A violation of the house rules is punished with a formal warning."},{"de":"Das Unternehmen muss wegen eines Verstoßes {{gegen}} das Datenschutzrecht zahlen.","en":"The company has to pay because of a breach of data protection law."},{"de":"Ein Verstoß {{gegen}} diese Regeln kann zum Ausschluss führen.","en":"A violation of these rules can lead to exclusion."}]},
 {"w":"die Neigung","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"tendency towards, inclination to","lv":"B2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu hat er eine Neigung? / Zu wem hat sie eine Neigung?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Verb: neigen zu. Also 'Neigung zu jemandem' = affection (rather literary).","ex":[{"de":"Er hat eine starke Neigung {{zu}} Übertreibungen.","en":"He has a strong tendency to exaggerate."},{"de":"Die Neigung {{zu}} Allergien ist teilweise erblich.","en":"The predisposition to allergies is partly hereditary."},{"de":"Ihre Neigung {{zu}} spitzen Bemerkungen machte sie unbeliebt.","en":"Her tendency to make sharp remarks made her unpopular."}]},
 {"w":"die Tendenz","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"tendency towards, trend towards","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu gibt es eine Tendenz?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","in + Dat."],"note":"Verb: tendieren zu.","ex":[{"de":"Es gibt eine deutliche Tendenz {{zu}} kürzeren Arbeitszeiten.","en":"There is a clear trend towards shorter working hours."},{"de":"Der Markt zeigt eine Tendenz {{zu}} Preissenkungen.","en":"The market shows a tendency towards price cuts."},{"de":"Die Tendenz {{zu}} immer größeren Bildschirmen ist ungebrochen.","en":"The trend towards ever larger screens continues unabated."}]},
 {"w":"der Appell","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"appeal to","lv":"C1","da":"daran","wo":"Woran appelliert sie? / An wen richtet sich der Appell?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","nach + Dat."],"note":"The addressee (or the value appealed to) takes an + Akk. Verb: appellieren an.","ex":[{"de":"Der Präsident richtete einen Appell {{an}} die Bevölkerung, ruhig zu bleiben.","en":"The president made an appeal to the population to stay calm."},{"de":"Mit einem Appell {{an}} die Vernunft versuchte sie, den Streit zu beenden.","en":"She tried to end the quarrel with an appeal to reason."},{"de":"Der Appell {{an}} die Eltern blieb weitgehend ungehört.","en":"The appeal to the parents went largely unheard."}]},
 {"w":"das Bekenntnis","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"commitment to, declaration of allegiance to","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu bekennt man sich? / Zu wem bekennt er sich?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Akk.","auf + Dat.","in + Akk."],"note":"Verb: sich bekennen zu.","ex":[{"de":"Das Bekenntnis {{zu}} demokratischen Werten ist Teil der Satzung.","en":"The commitment to democratic values is part of the statutes."},{"de":"Sie legte ein klares Bekenntnis {{zu}} ihrer Heimat ab.","en":"She made a clear declaration of loyalty to her homeland."},{"de":"Mit dem Bekenntnis {{zu}} diesem Bündnis wollte die Regierung Verlässlichkeit zeigen.","en":"With its commitment to this alliance the government wanted to show reliability."}]},
 {"w":"die Skepsis","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"scepticism towards","lv":"C1","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber herrscht Skepsis? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["vor + Dat.","für + Akk.","zu + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Adjective: skeptisch gegenüber.","ex":[{"de":"Viele Wähler äußern Skepsis {{gegenüber}} den Versprechen der Regierung.","en":"Many voters express scepticism towards the government's promises."},{"de":"Ihre Skepsis {{gegenüber}} dem neuen System war nicht unbegründet.","en":"Her scepticism towards the new system was not unfounded."},{"de":"Mit gesunder Skepsis {{gegenüber}} Werbeversprechen kauft man klüger ein.","en":"With a healthy scepticism towards advertising claims you shop more wisely."}]},
 {"w":"das Misstrauen","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"distrust of, mistrust towards","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber besteht Misstrauen? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["vor + Dat.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"alt":["gegen + Akk."],"note":"Both 'Misstrauen gegenüber' (+ Dat.) and 'Misstrauen gegen' (+ Akk.) are correct.","ex":[{"de":"Sein Misstrauen {{gegenüber}} Fremden war schwer zu überwinden.","en":"His distrust of strangers was hard to overcome."},{"de":"Nach dem Skandal wuchs das Misstrauen {{gegenüber}} den Banken.","en":"After the scandal, distrust of the banks grew."},{"de":"Ich hege ein tiefes Misstrauen {{gegenüber}} solchen Versprechungen.","en":"I harbour a deep distrust of such promises."}]},
 {"w":"die Verantwortung","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"responsibility towards (whom one answers to)","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber trägt man Verantwortung? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zu + Dat.","nach + Dat.","mit + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"sense":"towards someone","note":"gegenüber = to whom you are answerable; für = what you are responsible for (Verantwortung für die Folgen).","ex":[{"de":"Eltern tragen Verantwortung {{gegenüber}} ihren Kindern.","en":"Parents bear responsibility towards their children."},{"de":"Der Vorstand hat eine Verantwortung {{gegenüber}} den Aktionären.","en":"The board has a responsibility towards the shareholders."},{"de":"Wir haben eine besondere Verantwortung {{gegenüber}} kommenden Generationen.","en":"We have a special responsibility towards coming generations."}],"alt":["vor + Dat."]},
 {"w":"die Toleranz","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"tolerance towards","lv":"C1","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber zeigt man Toleranz? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zu + Dat.","über + Akk.","an + Dat.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Adjective: tolerant gegenüber. Also correct: Toleranz gegen + Akk.","ex":[{"de":"Die Toleranz {{gegenüber}} Andersdenkenden gehört zu den Grundwerten.","en":"Tolerance towards people who think differently is one of the basic values."},{"de":"Das Unternehmen zeigt keine Toleranz {{gegenüber}} Diskriminierung.","en":"The company shows no tolerance towards discrimination."},{"de":"Ihre Toleranz {{gegenüber}} Lärm hat Grenzen.","en":"Her tolerance of noise has limits."}],"alt":["gegen + Akk."]},
 {"w":"die Gleichgültigkeit","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"indifference towards","lv":"C1","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber zeigt er Gleichgültigkeit? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"ex":[{"de":"Die Gleichgültigkeit {{gegenüber}} dem Leid anderer erschreckte sie.","en":"The indifference towards other people's suffering frightened her."},{"de":"Seine Gleichgültigkeit {{gegenüber}} der Umwelt ist unverantwortlich.","en":"His indifference towards the environment is irresponsible."},{"de":"Politische Gleichgültigkeit {{gegenüber}} wichtigen Themen schwächt die Demokratie.","en":"Political indifference to important issues weakens democracy."}]},
 {"w":"die Anforderung","kind":"n","prep":"an","case":"Akk","en":"requirement for, demand on","lv":"B2","da":"daran","wo":"Woran werden Anforderungen gestellt? / An wen werden Anforderungen gestellt?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Typical: Anforderungen stellen an + Akk.; hohe Anforderungen an jemanden.","ex":[{"de":"Die Anforderungen {{an}} die Bewerber sind in dieser Branche hoch.","en":"The requirements for applicants are high in this industry."},{"de":"Neue Gesetze stellen strengere Anforderungen {{an}} den Datenschutz.","en":"New laws set stricter requirements for data protection."},{"de":"Das Gebäude erfüllt alle Anforderungen {{an}} den Brandschutz.","en":"The building meets all fire-safety requirements."}]},
 {"w":"der Einwand","kind":"n","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"objection to","lv":"B2","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen hat er einen Einwand? / Gegen wen richtet sich der Einwand?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","über + Akk."],"note":"Typical: einen Einwand erheben / haben gegen …; Einwände vorbringen.","ex":[{"de":"Haben Sie einen Einwand {{gegen}} diesen Vorschlag?","en":"Do you have an objection to this proposal?"},{"de":"Sein Einwand {{gegen}} die Zeitplanung wurde berücksichtigt.","en":"His objection to the schedule was taken into account."},{"de":"Es gibt keine Einwände {{gegen}} eine Verschiebung des Termins.","en":"There are no objections to postponing the appointment."}]},
 {"w":"der Anreiz","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"incentive for","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür schafft man einen Anreiz? / Für wen ist das ein Anreiz?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","nach + Dat.","über + Akk."],"alt":["zu + Dat."],"note":"With things/actions both 'Anreiz für' and 'Anreiz zu' occur (Anreiz zum Sparen); with persons only 'für'.","ex":[{"de":"Steuervorteile schaffen einen Anreiz {{für}} Investitionen.","en":"Tax breaks create an incentive for investment."},{"de":"Ohne finanzielle Anreize {{für}} Überstunden bleibt die Motivation gering.","en":"Without financial incentives for overtime, motivation stays low."},{"de":"Der Bonus ist ein starker Anreiz {{für}} längere Arbeitszeiten.","en":"The bonus is a strong incentive for longer working hours."}]},
 {"w":"die Befugnis","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"authority to, power to","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu hat er die Befugnis?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","mit + Dat."],"note":"Official language; often in the plural (Befugnisse). Adjective: befugt zu / befugt, etwas zu tun.","ex":[{"de":"Die Behörde hat die Befugnis {{zu}} Hausdurchsuchungen.","en":"The authority has the power to carry out house searches."},{"de":"Ihm fehlt jede Befugnis {{zu}} solchen Entscheidungen.","en":"He lacks any authority to make such decisions."},{"de":"Mit der Vollmacht erhielt er die Befugnis {{zu}} Verhandlungen im Namen der Firma.","en":"With the power of attorney he received the authority to negotiate on behalf of the company."}]},
 {"w":"die Anspielung","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"allusion to, hint at","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf ist das eine Anspielung? / Auf wen spielt er an?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","zu + Dat.","über + Akk.","an + Akk."],"note":"Verb: anspielen auf.","ex":[{"de":"Seine Bemerkung war eine Anspielung {{auf}} die Affäre vom Vorjahr.","en":"His remark was an allusion to last year's affair."},{"de":"Sie verstand die Anspielung {{auf}} ihr Alter sofort.","en":"She understood the dig at her age immediately."},{"de":"Der Film steckt voller Anspielungen {{auf}} berühmte Klassiker.","en":"The film is full of allusions to famous classics."}]},
 {"w":"die Aussicht","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"prospect of","lv":"B2","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf hat man Aussicht?","decoys":["an + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","um + Akk."],"note":"The 'view' meaning also takes auf + Akk.: die Aussicht auf den See.","ex":[{"de":"Die Aussicht {{auf}} einen Job im Ausland motivierte ihn.","en":"The prospect of a job abroad motivated him."},{"de":"Es besteht keine Aussicht {{auf}} eine baldige Einigung.","en":"There is no prospect of an early agreement."},{"de":"Die Aussicht {{auf}} eine Gehaltserhöhung hält ihn in der Firma.","en":"The prospect of a pay rise keeps him at the company."}]},
 {"w":"der Widerstand","kind":"n","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"resistance to, opposition to","lv":"B2","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen leistet man Widerstand? / Gegen wen leistet man Widerstand?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Typical: Widerstand leisten gegen.","ex":[{"de":"Der Widerstand {{gegen}} das Bauprojekt wächst.","en":"Opposition to the building project is growing."},{"de":"Die Bevölkerung leistete Widerstand {{gegen}} die Besatzer.","en":"The population put up resistance against the occupiers."},{"de":"Es gab heftigen Widerstand {{gegen}} die geplante Gesetzesänderung.","en":"There was fierce opposition to the planned change in the law."}]},
 {"w":"das Vorgehen","kind":"n","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"action against, measures against","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen geht man vor? / Gegen wen richtet sich das Vorgehen?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Verb: vorgehen gegen.","ex":[{"de":"Das konsequente Vorgehen {{gegen}} Steuerbetrug zahlt sich aus.","en":"Consistent action against tax fraud pays off."},{"de":"Die Regierung kündigte ein hartes Vorgehen {{gegen}} illegale Müllkippen an.","en":"The government announced tough action against illegal dumps."},{"de":"Ihr Vorgehen {{gegen}} den Konkurrenten blieb nicht ohne Folgen.","en":"Her moves against the competitor did not go without consequences."}]},
 {"w":"die Anfälligkeit","kind":"n","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"susceptibility to, proneness to","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür zeigt das System eine hohe Anfälligkeit?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Adjective: anfällig für.","ex":[{"de":"Die Anfälligkeit {{für}} Infektionen steigt im Alter.","en":"Susceptibility to infections rises with age."},{"de":"Das System zeigt eine hohe Anfälligkeit {{für}} Hackerangriffe.","en":"The system shows a high vulnerability to hacker attacks."},{"de":"Eine erhöhte Anfälligkeit {{für}} Stress kann erblich bedingt sein.","en":"An increased susceptibility to stress can be hereditary."}]},
 {"w":"die Fixierung","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"fixation on, fixedness on","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf ist man fixiert? / Auf wen ist sie fixiert?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","für + Akk.","zu + Dat.","in + Akk."],"note":"Verb: sich fixieren auf; adjective: fixiert auf.","ex":[{"de":"Die Fixierung {{auf}} Leistung prägt das gesamte Schulsystem.","en":"The fixation on performance shapes the whole school system."},{"de":"Seine Fixierung {{auf}} Geld ist beängstigend.","en":"His fixation on money is frightening."},{"de":"Eine zu starke Fixierung {{auf}} das Smartphone schadet der Konzentration.","en":"Too strong a fixation on the smartphone harms concentration."}]},
 {"w":"die Spezialisierung","kind":"n","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"specialisation in","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf hat sie sich spezialisiert?","decoys":["an + Dat.","über + Akk.","nach + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Verb: sich spezialisieren auf.","ex":[{"de":"Die Spezialisierung {{auf}} Nischenprodukte sicherte der Firma das Überleben.","en":"Specialising in niche products secured the firm's survival."},{"de":"Nach dem Studium folgte die Spezialisierung {{auf}} Kinderchirurgie.","en":"After graduating came specialisation in paediatric surgery."},{"de":"Ihre Spezialisierung {{auf}} Umweltrecht macht sie sehr gefragt.","en":"Her specialisation in environmental law makes her much sought after."}]},
 {"w":"die Zugehörigkeit","kind":"n","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"membership of, affiliation with, sense of belonging to","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu gehört man? / Zu wem gehört man?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Dat.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Verb: gehören zu.","ex":[{"de":"Die Zugehörigkeit {{zu}} einer Gruppe gibt vielen Menschen Halt.","en":"Belonging to a group gives many people stability."},{"de":"Seine Zugehörigkeit {{zu}} einer verbotenen Partei wurde ihm zum Verhängnis.","en":"His membership of a banned party proved his undoing."},{"de":"Das Gefühl der Zugehörigkeit {{zu}} einer Gemeinschaft ist für Jugendliche wichtig.","en":"The feeling of belonging to a community is important for young people."}]},
 {"w":"die Haltung","kind":"n","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"attitude towards","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber hat sie eine kritische Haltung? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","über + Akk.","mit + Dat."],"alt":["zu + Dat."],"note":"'Haltung zu' (+ Dat.) is equally correct, esp. for topics: seine Haltung zur Atomkraft.","ex":[{"de":"Ihre Haltung {{gegenüber}} der neuen Technik ist eher kritisch.","en":"Her attitude towards the new technology is rather critical."},{"de":"Die Haltung der Regierung {{gegenüber}} den Reformen sorgte für Streit.","en":"The government's attitude towards the reforms caused a dispute."},{"de":"Eine offene Haltung {{gegenüber}} Veränderungen hilft im Beruf.","en":"An open attitude to change helps in your career."}]},
 {"w":"anfällig","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"susceptible to, prone to","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das System anfällig?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","zu + Dat.","vor + Dat.","an + Dat."],"note":"Noun: die Anfälligkeit für.","ex":[{"de":"Alte Systeme sind besonders anfällig {{für}} Fehler.","en":"Old systems are particularly prone to errors."},{"de":"Kinder sind im Winter anfällig {{für}} Erkältungen.","en":"Children are susceptible to colds in winter."},{"de":"Diese Pflanze ist anfällig {{für}} Pilzbefall.","en":"This plant is prone to fungal infestation."}]},
 {"w":"empfänglich","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"receptive to, susceptible to","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist er empfänglich?","decoys":["auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","zu + Dat.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Can be positive (receptive to) or negative (open to manipulation).","ex":[{"de":"Er ist empfänglich {{für}} Schmeicheleien.","en":"He is susceptible to flattery."},{"de":"Jugendliche sind oft empfänglich {{für}} radikale Ideen.","en":"Young people are often receptive to radical ideas."},{"de":"Das Publikum zeigte sich empfänglich {{für}} ihre Botschaft.","en":"The audience proved receptive to her message."}]},
 {"w":"bewandert","kind":"a","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"well-versed in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin ist sie bewandert?","decoys":["in + Akk.","an + Dat.","mit + Dat.","über + Akk."],"note":"Rather formal/literary; similar: versiert in, erfahren in.","ex":[{"de":"Sie ist {{in}} der Geschichte der Region bestens bewandert.","en":"She is thoroughly versed in the history of the region."},{"de":"Er ist {{in}} Rechtsfragen erstaunlich bewandert.","en":"He is amazingly knowledgeable in legal matters."},{"de":"Als Archäologin ist sie {{in}} antiken Sprachen bewandert.","en":"As an archaeologist she is well versed in ancient languages."}]},
 {"w":"erpicht","kind":"a","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"keen on, eager for","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf ist er erpicht?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","für + Akk.","an + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Often negated or ironic: nicht erpicht darauf, dass …","ex":[{"de":"Er war nicht gerade {{auf}} ein Gespräch mit dem Chef erpicht.","en":"He was not exactly keen on a conversation with the boss."},{"de":"Die Firma ist {{auf}} neue Aufträge erpicht.","en":"The company is eager for new orders."},{"de":"Sie war nie {{auf}} Ruhm erpicht.","en":"She was never after fame."}]},
 {"w":"erhaben","kind":"a","prep":"über","case":"Akk","en":"above, superior to","lv":"C1","da":"darüber","wo":"Worüber ist er erhaben? / Über wen ist er erhaben?","decoys":["über + Dat.","vor + Dat.","gegen + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"Fixed phrase: über jeden Zweifel / über jede Kritik erhaben.","ex":[{"de":"Seine Integrität ist {{über}} jeden Zweifel erhaben.","en":"His integrity is beyond any doubt."},{"de":"Sie fühlte sich {{über}} solche Kleinlichkeiten erhaben.","en":"She felt above such pettiness."},{"de":"Kein Politiker ist {{über}} jede Kritik erhaben.","en":"No politician is above all criticism."}]},
 {"w":"behaftet","kind":"a","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"afflicted with, laden with (flaws, uncertainties)","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit ist es behaftet?","decoys":["mit + Akk.","von + Dat.","durch + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Always negative: mit Fehlern / Mängeln / Risiken behaftet.","ex":[{"de":"Das Verfahren ist {{mit}} erheblichen Mängeln behaftet.","en":"The procedure is beset by considerable flaws."},{"de":"Der Neubau war {{mit}} zahlreichen Fehlern behaftet.","en":"The new building was riddled with numerous faults."},{"de":"Die Studie bleibt {{mit}} Unsicherheiten behaftet.","en":"The study remains fraught with uncertainties."}]},
 {"w":"vereinbar","kind":"a","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"compatible with, consistent with","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit ist das vereinbar?","decoys":["mit + Akk.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Opposite: unvereinbar mit. Noun: die Vereinbarkeit von Familie und Beruf.","ex":[{"de":"Dieses Verhalten ist nicht {{mit}} den Unternehmenswerten vereinbar.","en":"This behaviour is not compatible with the company's values."},{"de":"Ist dieser Plan {{mit}} dem Grundgesetz vereinbar?","en":"Is this plan compatible with the Basic Law?"},{"de":"Teilzeitarbeit ist {{mit}} einer Führungsposition schwer vereinbar.","en":"Part-time work is hard to reconcile with a managerial position."}]},
 {"w":"verpflichtet","kind":"a","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"obliged to, committed to","lv":"B2","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu ist man verpflichtet?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","an + Dat.","mit + Dat."],"note":"To whom one is obliged: verpflichtet gegenüber (den Kunden). Noun: die Verpflichtung zu.","ex":[{"de":"Der Arzt ist {{zu}} Verschwiegenheit verpflichtet.","en":"The doctor is bound by a duty of confidentiality."},{"de":"Die Mieter sind {{zu}} regelmäßiger Treppenhausreinigung verpflichtet.","en":"The tenants are obliged to clean the stairwell regularly."},{"de":"Wir fühlen uns {{zu}} größter Sorgfalt verpflichtet.","en":"We feel obliged to exercise the greatest care."}]},
 {"w":"imstande","kind":"a","prep":"zu","case":"Dat","en":"capable of","lv":"C1","da":"dazu","wo":"Wozu ist er imstande?","decoys":["zu + Akk.","für + Akk.","an + Dat.","in + Dat."],"note":"Used with sein: imstande sein. Often followed by an infinitive clause instead: Er ist imstande, alles zu tun.","ex":[{"de":"Er ist {{zu}} jeder Gemeinheit imstande.","en":"He is capable of any meanness."},{"de":"Nach dem Unfall war sie {{zu}} keiner klaren Antwort imstande.","en":"After the accident she was incapable of giving a clear answer."},{"de":"Ich bin heute {{zu}} nichts mehr imstande.","en":"I'm not up to anything any more today."}]},
 {"w":"entscheidend","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"decisive for, crucial for","lv":"B2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das entscheidend? / Für wen ist das entscheidend?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Similar: ausschlaggebend für, maßgeblich für.","ex":[{"de":"Die Wahl der Methode ist entscheidend {{für}} den Erfolg.","en":"The choice of method is decisive for success."},{"de":"Der Zeitpunkt ist {{für}} den Verkauf entscheidend.","en":"The timing is crucial for the sale."},{"de":"Die Qualität der Zutaten ist entscheidend {{für}} den Geschmack.","en":"The quality of the ingredients is crucial for the taste."}]},
 {"w":"maßgeblich","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"authoritative for, decisive for","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das maßgeblich? / Für wen ist das maßgeblich?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Official register; synonym: maßgebend für.","ex":[{"de":"Das Gutachten war maßgeblich {{für}} die Entscheidung des Gerichts.","en":"The expert report was decisive for the court's decision."},{"de":"Maßgeblich {{für}} die Berechnung ist das Bruttoeinkommen.","en":"What counts for the calculation is the gross income."},{"de":"Die Rechtslage am Stichtag ist {{für}} den Anspruch maßgeblich.","en":"The legal situation on the cut-off date is decisive for the claim."}]},
 {"w":"förderlich","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"conducive to, beneficial for","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das förderlich? / Für wen ist das förderlich?","decoys":["über + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Can also take a plain dative: der Gesundheit förderlich. Opposite: hinderlich, abträglich.","ex":[{"de":"Regelmäßige Bewegung ist {{für}} die Gesundheit förderlich.","en":"Regular exercise is beneficial for your health."},{"de":"Ein gutes Betriebsklima ist förderlich {{für}} die Produktivität.","en":"A good working atmosphere is conducive to productivity."},{"de":"Diese Atmosphäre war {{für}} Kreativität nicht gerade förderlich.","en":"This atmosphere was not exactly conducive to creativity."}]},
 {"w":"nachteilig","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"disadvantageous for, detrimental to","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das nachteilig? / Für wen ist das nachteilig?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Opposite: vorteilhaft für. Noun: der Nachteil für.","ex":[{"de":"Die Maßnahme ist nachteilig {{für}} kleine Betriebe.","en":"The measure is disadvantageous for small businesses."},{"de":"Eine Verzögerung wäre {{für}} alle Beteiligten nachteilig.","en":"A delay would be detrimental to everyone involved."},{"de":"Der Vertrag erwies sich {{für}} den Käufer als nachteilig.","en":"The contract turned out to be disadvantageous for the buyer."}]},
 {"w":"kennzeichnend","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"characteristic of, distinctive of","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das kennzeichnend? / Für wen ist das kennzeichnend?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Verb: kennzeichnen (to characterise, to mark); similar: typisch für, charakteristisch für.","ex":[{"de":"Diese Bauweise ist kennzeichnend {{für}} die Region.","en":"This style of building is characteristic of the region."},{"de":"Kennzeichnend {{für}} seinen Stil ist der sparsame Einsatz von Farbe.","en":"Characteristic of his style is the sparing use of colour."},{"de":"Ein hohes Maß an Eigenverantwortung ist kennzeichnend {{für}} unsere Firmenkultur.","en":"A high degree of personal responsibility is characteristic of our company culture."}]},
 {"w":"charakteristisch","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"characteristic of","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist das charakteristisch? / Für wen ist das charakteristisch?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"Similar: typisch für, kennzeichnend für.","ex":[{"de":"Lange, kalte Winter sind charakteristisch {{für}} diese Region.","en":"Long, cold winters are characteristic of this region."},{"de":"Das ist ein Verhalten, das {{für}} Teenager charakteristisch ist.","en":"That is behaviour that is characteristic of teenagers."},{"de":"Charakteristisch {{für}} diese Pflanzenart sind die gezackten Blätter.","en":"Characteristic of this plant species are the serrated leaves."}]},
 {"w":"repräsentativ","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"representative of","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist die Umfrage repräsentativ? / Für wen ist sie repräsentativ?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","von + Dat.","auf + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Typical in statistics: eine repräsentative Umfrage.","ex":[{"de":"Die Umfrage ist nicht repräsentativ {{für}} die gesamte Bevölkerung.","en":"The survey is not representative of the whole population."},{"de":"Diese Stichprobe ist {{für}} Deutschland repräsentativ.","en":"This sample is representative of Germany."},{"de":"Seine Meinung ist kaum repräsentativ {{für}} die Stimmung im Land.","en":"His opinion is hardly representative of the mood in the country."}]},
 {"w":"immun","kind":"a","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"immune to","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen ist er immun?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","von + Dat."],"note":"Literal (medical) and figurative use. Noun: die Immunität gegen.","ex":[{"de":"Nach der Impfung ist man {{gegen}} das Virus immun.","en":"After the vaccination you are immune to the virus."},{"de":"Er ist {{gegen}} jede Form von Schmeichelei immun.","en":"He is immune to every form of flattery."},{"de":"Manche Menschen sind von Natur aus {{gegen}} Kälte nahezu immun.","en":"Some people are almost immune to cold by nature."}]},
 {"w":"resistent","kind":"a","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"resistant to","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen ist es resistent?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","für + Akk.","vor + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"alt":["gegenüber + Dat."],"note":"Both 'resistent gegen' (+ Akk.) and 'resistent gegenüber' (+ Dat.) are correct. Noun: die Resistenz.","ex":[{"de":"Viele Keime sind {{gegen}} Antibiotika resistent.","en":"Many germs are resistant to antibiotics."},{"de":"Die neue Sorte ist {{gegen}} Trockenheit resistent.","en":"The new variety is resistant to drought."},{"de":"Der Lack ist {{gegen}} Kratzer und Säuren resistent.","en":"The paint is resistant to scratches and acids."}]},
 {"w":"tolerant","kind":"a","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"tolerant towards","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber ist man tolerant? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","für + Akk.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Noun: die Toleranz gegenüber. Also correct: tolerant gegen + Akk.","ex":[{"de":"Er ist {{gegenüber}} anderen Meinungen sehr tolerant.","en":"He is very tolerant of other opinions."},{"de":"Unsere Firma ist {{gegenüber}} Fehlern recht tolerant.","en":"Our company is quite tolerant of mistakes."},{"de":"Man sollte {{gegenüber}} Minderheiten tolerant sein.","en":"One should be tolerant towards minorities."}],"alt":["gegen + Akk."]},
 {"w":"skeptisch","kind":"a","prep":"gegenüber","case":"Dat","en":"sceptical of, sceptical about","lv":"B2","da":"ihm / ihr / ihnen gegenüber (kein da-Kompositum)","wo":"Wem gegenüber ist sie skeptisch? (kein Wo-Kompositum)","decoys":["vor + Dat.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","an + Dat."],"note":"Noun: die Skepsis gegenüber.","ex":[{"de":"Sie ist {{gegenüber}} Versprechungen grundsätzlich skeptisch.","en":"She is sceptical of promises on principle."},{"de":"Die Experten sind {{gegenüber}} dem neuen Verfahren skeptisch.","en":"The experts are sceptical of the new procedure."},{"de":"Er blieb {{gegenüber}} allen Angeboten skeptisch.","en":"He remained sceptical of all the offers."}]},
 {"w":"aufgeschlossen","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"open to, receptive to","lv":"C1","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist sie aufgeschlossen?","decoys":["zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","über + Akk."],"alt":["gegenüber + Dat."],"note":"Both 'aufgeschlossen für' (+ Akk.) and 'aufgeschlossen gegenüber' (+ Dat.) are correct.","ex":[{"de":"Sie ist sehr aufgeschlossen {{für}} neue Ideen.","en":"She is very open to new ideas."},{"de":"Unser Team ist {{für}} Veränderungen aufgeschlossen.","en":"Our team is open to change."},{"de":"Der Chef zeigte sich {{für}} Vorschläge der Mitarbeiter aufgeschlossen.","en":"The boss proved receptive to the staff's suggestions."}]},
 {"w":"zugänglich","kind":"a","prep":"für","case":"Akk","en":"accessible to; open to","lv":"B2","da":"dafür","wo":"Wofür ist es zugänglich? / Für wen ist es zugänglich?","decoys":["an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk.","vor + Dat."],"note":"Also with a plain dative (figurative): seinen Argumenten nicht zugänglich.","ex":[{"de":"Das Museum ist auch {{für}} Rollstuhlfahrer zugänglich.","en":"The museum is also accessible to wheelchair users."},{"de":"Er ist {{für}} Kritik nicht zugänglich.","en":"He is not receptive to criticism."},{"de":"Die Daten sind {{für}} die Öffentlichkeit frei zugänglich.","en":"The data are freely accessible to the public."}]},
 {"w":"beteiligt","kind":"a","prep":"an","case":"Dat","en":"involved in, participating in; having a stake in","lv":"B2","da":"daran","wo":"Woran ist sie beteiligt?","decoys":["an + Akk.","für + Akk.","auf + Akk.","gegen + Akk."],"note":"Verb: sich beteiligen an; noun: die Beteiligung an.","ex":[{"de":"Sie war {{an}} dem Unfall nicht beteiligt.","en":"She was not involved in the accident."},{"de":"Mehrere Firmen sind {{an}} diesem Projekt beteiligt.","en":"Several companies are involved in this project."},{"de":"Er ist mit 20 Prozent {{an}} der Firma beteiligt.","en":"He holds a 20 percent stake in the company."}]},
 {"w":"betroffen","kind":"a","prep":"von","case":"Dat","en":"affected by","lv":"B2","da":"davon","wo":"Wovon ist die Region betroffen?","decoys":["von + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"betroffen von = affected by; 'betroffen über' = shaken/dismayed at (zutiefst betroffen über den Tod).","ex":[{"de":"Viele Haushalte sind {{von}} der Preiserhöhung betroffen.","en":"Many households are affected by the price increase."},{"de":"Die Region ist besonders stark {{von}} der Dürre betroffen.","en":"The region is particularly badly affected by the drought."},{"de":"Wer ist {{von}} der neuen Regelung betroffen?","en":"Who is affected by the new rule?"}]},
 {"w":"gefasst","kind":"a","prep":"auf","case":"Akk","en":"prepared for, braced for","lv":"C1","da":"darauf","wo":"Worauf ist man gefasst?","decoys":["auf + Dat.","für + Akk.","vor + Dat.","an + Akk."],"note":"Almost always with sein: auf etwas gefasst sein; also sich auf etwas gefasst machen.","ex":[{"de":"Wir sind {{auf}} das Schlimmste gefasst.","en":"We are prepared for the worst."},{"de":"Sie war nicht {{auf}} eine solche Reaktion gefasst.","en":"She wasn't prepared for such a reaction."},{"de":"Man muss {{auf}} Verzögerungen gefasst sein.","en":"You have to be prepared for delays."}]},
 {"w":"ausgestattet","kind":"a","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"equipped with, endowed with","lv":"B2","da":"damit","wo":"Womit ist es ausgestattet?","decoys":["mit + Akk.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk.","zu + Dat."],"note":"Verb: ausstatten mit; noun: die Ausstattung.","ex":[{"de":"Das Zimmer ist {{mit}} einer modernen Klimaanlage ausgestattet.","en":"The room is equipped with a modern air-conditioning system."},{"de":"Der Beauftragte wurde {{mit}} umfassenden Befugnissen ausgestattet.","en":"The commissioner was endowed with extensive powers."},{"de":"Die Schule ist {{mit}} Tablets für alle Schüler ausgestattet.","en":"The school is equipped with tablets for all pupils."}]},
 {"w":"gleichbedeutend","kind":"a","prep":"mit","case":"Dat","en":"synonymous with, tantamount to","lv":"C1","da":"damit","wo":"Womit ist es gleichbedeutend?","decoys":["mit + Akk.","zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Similar: gleichzusetzen mit, gleichzustellen mit.","ex":[{"de":"Ein Rücktritt wäre {{mit}} einem Eingeständnis gleichbedeutend.","en":"A resignation would be tantamount to an admission."},{"de":"Stillstand ist in dieser Branche {{mit}} Rückschritt gleichbedeutend.","en":"In this industry standing still is tantamount to going backwards."},{"de":"Für viele ist Erfolg {{mit}} Geld gleichbedeutend.","en":"For many people success is synonymous with money."}]},
 {"w":"geprägt","kind":"a","prep":"von","case":"Dat","en":"marked by, shaped by","lv":"B2","da":"davon","wo":"Wovon ist es geprägt? / Von wem ist er geprägt?","decoys":["von + Akk.","zu + Dat.","an + Dat.","für + Akk."],"alt":["durch + Akk."],"note":"Both 'geprägt von' (+ Dat.) and 'geprägt durch' (+ Akk.) are correct.","ex":[{"de":"Seine Kindheit war {{von}} Armut geprägt.","en":"His childhood was marked by poverty."},{"de":"Das Stadtbild ist {{von}} Gebäuden aus dem 19. Jahrhundert geprägt.","en":"The cityscape is shaped by buildings from the 19th century."},{"de":"Die Debatte ist {{von}} Misstrauen geprägt.","en":"The debate is characterised by mistrust."}]},
 {"w":"verwurzelt","kind":"a","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"rooted in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin ist es verwurzelt?","decoys":["in + Akk.","zu + Dat.","für + Akk.","über + Akk."],"note":"State, so dative: in der Tradition verwurzelt. Verb: sich verwurzeln.","ex":[{"de":"Der Brauch ist tief {{in}} der Region verwurzelt.","en":"The custom is deeply rooted in the region."},{"de":"Sie ist fest {{in}} ihrer Heimatstadt verwurzelt.","en":"She is firmly rooted in her home town."},{"de":"Diese Vorurteile sind {{in}} der Gesellschaft tief verwurzelt.","en":"These prejudices are deeply rooted in society."}]},
 {"w":"gefeit","kind":"a","prep":"gegen","case":"Akk","en":"immune to, proof against","lv":"C1","da":"dagegen","wo":"Wogegen ist man gefeit?","decoys":["gegen + Dat.","für + Akk.","von + Dat.","auf + Akk."],"note":"Literary/formal; mostly in the phrase gegen etwas gefeit sein.","ex":[{"de":"Kein Politiker ist {{gegen}} Versuchungen völlig gefeit.","en":"No politician is completely proof against temptation."},{"de":"Niemand ist {{gegen}} Irrtümer gefeit.","en":"Nobody is immune to error."},{"de":"Sie fühlte sich {{gegen}} jede Kritik gefeit.","en":"She felt immune to any criticism."}]},
 {"w":"versiert","kind":"a","prep":"in","case":"Dat","en":"skilled in, experienced in","lv":"C1","da":"darin","wo":"Worin ist er versiert?","decoys":["in + Akk.","zu + Dat.","über + Akk.","für + Akk."],"note":"Similar: bewandert in, erfahren in.","ex":[{"de":"Der Anwalt ist {{in}} Steuerfragen äußerst versiert.","en":"The lawyer is extremely skilled in tax matters."},{"de":"Sie ist {{in}} mehreren Programmiersprachen versiert.","en":"She is proficient in several programming languages."},{"de":"Er gilt als versiert {{in}} der Verhandlungsführung.","en":"He is regarded as experienced in conducting negotiations."}]}
